    "https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/53358": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Accounting",
      "description": "Montana State University Employment Opportunities | Assistant Professor of Accounting Skip to Main Content Jobs at Montana State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About MSU About Bozeman Benefits Academics Assistant Professor of Accounting Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Required Application Documents: Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter addressing how you meet each individual required qualification and, as applicable, each preferred qualification Teaching statement (maximum two pages) Research statement (maximum two pages) References : All applicants will be required to provide a minimum of three references during the application process. References will be contacted by phone as part of the final reference check process after on-campus interviews. Position Details Position Information Announcement Number FAC - VA - 27027 For questions regarding this position, please contact: Sean Harris Associate Professor sean.harris1@montana.edu Classification Title Working Title Assistant Professor of Accounting Brief Position Overview The Jake Jabs College of Business & Entrepreneurship at Montana State University invites applications for a tenure-track position in accounting. We seek candidates who are dedicated to excellence in the classroom, to producing impactful research, and who will thrive in our rich, mountainous environment. Candidates with the ability to teach in multiple areas of accounting are particularly encouraged to apply. Faculty Tenure Track Yes Faculty Rank Assistant Professor Position Number 4A0631 Department Jabs College of Business Instruct Division College of Business Appointment Type Faculty Contract Term Academic Year Semester If other, specify From date If other, specify End date Union Affiliation Exempt from Collective Bargaining FTE 1.0 Benefits Eligible Eligible Salary Salary commensurate with experience, education, and qualifications Contract Type MUS If other, please specify Recruitment Type Open Position Details General Statement The Jake Jabs College of Business & Entrepreneurship invites applications for a tenure-track position to join the College’s Accounting program. We seek candidates who are excellent at imparting state-of-the-art accounting knowledge to students from all socioeconomic, geographical, and ideological backgrounds. Candidates with the ability to teach in multiple areas of accounting are particularly encouraged to apply. We seek candidates who will deliver excellence in the classroom, produce quality, impactful research, and who will thrive in our rich, mountainous environment. Montana State University values all perspectives and is committed to continually supporting, promoting and building a whole community, which includes people of many backgrounds. We hope to attract applicants who can teach in a University community and have demonstrated ability in helping students from all backgrounds to succeed. Duties and Responsibilities The accounting program offers an accounting undergraduate concentration as part of a BS in Business degree, and a Master of Professional Accountancy degree. The successful candidate must be willing and able to provide effective, high-quality instruction in multiple accounting courses at the bachelor’s and master’s levels, with a normal teaching load of 15 credit hours per year. In addition, the successful candidate will advise students, conduct scholarly research, and provide college and university service and engagement. Faculty members are expected to publish impactful research in quality, peer-reviewed journals related to the accounting field. Required Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills Ph. D or D.B.A. degree with emphasis in accounting or a closely related field by start date. Potential to teach undergraduate and graduate courses in accounting. Potential to carry on a successful program of scholarly research resulting in publication in quality peer-reviewed journals. Preferred Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills Demonstrated experience providing high-quality teaching in a variety of accounting areas. Demonstrated evidence of an active research program in accounting, with current projects targeting publication in high-quality peer-reviewed journals. Relevant professional accounting experience. Relevant professional accounting certifications. The Successful Candidate Will Be committed to excellence in teaching. Have effective oral and written communication skills. Have the ability to establish and maintain productive working relationships with colleagues and students. Be committed to service and engagement in the college, the university, the accounting profession, and the community. Be dedicated to supporting and enhancing Montana State University’s commitment to continually supporting, promoting and building a whole community, which includes people of many backgrounds. Position Special Requirements/Additional Information To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. The requirements listed above are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. Physical Demands To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. The requirements listed above are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. The Program The accounting program falls under the Accounting and Finance Department and offers an accounting undergraduate concentration as part of a BS in Business degree, and a Master of Professional Accountancy degree. The Department The Accounting and Finance Department consists of 11 tenure-track track faculty and offers both accounting and finance undergraduate concentrations as part of a BS in Business degree, and a Master of Professional Accountancy degree. The College The Jake Jabs College of Business & Entrepreneurship offers a B.S. in Business with options in Accounting, Finance, Hospitality Management, Management, and Marketing, an M.S. in Innovation and Management, and a Master of Professional Accountancy degree. The College has 31 tenure-track faculty who are augmented by an experienced group of professionally qualified instructors. Faculty members enjoy a collegial environment and are committed to excellence in business education. The combination of a positive professional work environment and outstanding outdoor recreational opportunities offers a uniquely satisfying lifestyle. Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date August 2027 Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Close Date Applications will be: Screening of applications will begin on November 12, 2026 ; however, applications will continue to be accepted until an adequate applicant pool has been established. Special Instructions Required Application Documents: Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter addressing how you meet each individual required qualification and, as applicable, each preferred qualification Teaching statement (maximum two pages) Research statement (maximum two pages) References : All applicants will be required to provide a minimum of three references during the application process. References will be contacted by phone as part of the final reference check process after on-campus interviews. EEO Statement Montana State University is an equal opportunity employer. MSU does not discriminate against any applicant on the basis of race, color, religion, creed, political ideas, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, marital status, national origin, physical or mental disability, or any other protected class status in violation of any applicable law. In compliance with the Montana Veteran’s Employment Preference Act, MSU provides preference in employment to veterans, disabled veterans, and certain eligible relatives of veterans. To claim veteran’s preference, please complete the veteran’s preference information located in the Demographics section of your profile. FLSA Details FLSA Determination FLSA Status Exempt Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Research Statement Teaching Statement Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). University Human Resources 920 Technology BLVD, Suite A Bozeman, MT 59718 406-994-3651 humanresources@montana.edu Accessibility | Contact List | Directories | Jobs | Legal & Privacy Policy | Site Index Montana State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/53352": {
      "title": "Agricultural and Technology Education Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool)",
      "description": "Montana State University Employment Opportunities | Agricultural and Technology Education Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) Skip to Main Content Jobs at Montana State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About MSU About Bozeman Benefits Academics Agricultural and Technology Education Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This position is not eligible for new sponsorship. Review of applications will be on a continual basis and will continue until the position(s) are filled. Applicants are retained in the hiring pool for up to two years. Position Details Position Information Announcement Number FAC - VA - 26081 For questions regarding this position, please contact: Andrew Thomson andrew.thomson1@montana.edu (406) 994-2132 Classification Title Instructor Working Title Agricultural and Technology Education Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) Brief Position Overview Faculty Tenure Track No Faculty Rank Non-Tenure Track Position Number 4A6112 Department Agricultural Education Division College of Agriculture/MAES Appointment Type Non-Tenure Track (Pooled) Contract Term Other Semester Fall or Spring If other, specify From date If other, specify End date Union Affiliation Contact HR for Determination FTE Varies Benefits Eligible Depends on FTE (please contact Human Resources - 406-994-3651) Salary Salary commensurate with experience, education, and qualifications Contract Type LOA If other, please specify Recruitment Type Open Position Details General Statement Montana State University seeks qualified individuals to provide non-tenurable level instruction and/or related functions. Instructors are needed to teach classes depending upon need and available funding. Applications are accepted on a continual basis (unless otherwise indicated) and will be maintained in pool for two years. After two years, candidates will be notified to re-submit materials for continued consideration. The department or program search committees or hiring authority will review and evaluate the submitted application materials. Applicants will be notified if their application is being retained in the non-tenure track faculty hiring pool. Appointments are on a part-time basis and vary in duration, a couple weeks, a semester or an academic year, depending on the specific needs of the department/program. Salary is dependent on number of courses taught and duration. We seek individuals who work professionally and effectively with all individuals, possess effective interpersonal, written and verbal communication skills and have the ability to contribute positively to the academic success of the students and the mission of Montana State University. Duties and Responsibilities Teaching on-campus or online courses. Advising, evaluating and assisting students. Participating in Departmental faculty meetings and other Departmental functions. Required Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills BS Degree in Agricultural Education, Technology Education, or other field relevant to the position. Preferred Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills MS Degree. Prior teaching experience directly related to the position for which you are applying. Experience teaching face-to-face, hybrid, and online courses using a Learning Management System. Demonstrated experience teaching interdisciplinary courses. Demonstrated knowledge of college student development. The Successful Candidate Will Have the ability to relate to students and to develop classroom rapport with students. Have the ability to work effectively with a wide range of student populations. Have effective interpersonal skills including the ability to collaborate successfully with faculty and staff. Possess excellent written and oral communication skills. Be skilled in utilizing engaging pedagogy that involves students in the learning process. Take initiative and work well independently. Possess the ability to learn material quickly and adapt to changing environments. Position Special Requirements/Additional Information The position for which you have applied MAY BE a Union position. Union affiliation is determined by job duties and the collective bargaining unit. Non-Tenure Track Faculty – Any position that is .5 FTE or more is represented by the Associated Faculty of Montana State University ( AFMSU ). Faculty covered by AFMSU may choose to pay membership dues. This is a condition of employment. Additional information can be found at AFMSU or by emailing AFSMU . Any position less than .5 FTE is not represented by the Union and is not required to pay dues. If the FTE changes during employment, the representational status of this position could be impacted. Exceptions: Anyone having successfully completed a PEI exam or any faculty working in Extension are exempt from the Union. This job description should not be construed as an exhaustive statement of duties, responsibilities or requirements, but a general description of the job. Nothing contained herein restricts Montana State University’s rights to assign or reassign duties and responsibilities to this job at any time. Physical Demands To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. The requirements listed above are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. The Program The Department The Department of Agricultural & Technology Education is housed within the College of Agriculture and has 6 faculty/staff members. The Department is dedicated to serving the needs of all students and stakeholders through a dynamic and comprehensive program of rural leadership, technological advancement, and proven scientific and educational practices. The program is grounded in basic and applied research aimed at improving professional and technical skills through formal and non-formal education in agriculture and industrial technology. The Department offers two degree programs with two major options in each program: Agricultural Education; Broadfield Teaching or Communications, Leadership and Extension. Applied Technology Management; Broadfield Teaching or Industry Option, as well as a teaching minor in Technology Education. The Department offers both an on-campus and online Master’s degree. The College As the foundation of the land grant mission at Montana State University, the College of Agriculture and the Montana Agricultural Experiment Station provide instruction in traditional and innovative degree programs and conduct research on old and new challenges for Montana’s agricultural community. This integration creates opportunities for students and faculty to excel through hands-on learning, to serve through campus and community engagement, to explore unique solutions to distinct and interesting questions and to connect Montanans with the global community through research discoveries and outreach. Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies Multiple Positions Desired Start Date Review of applications will be on a continual basis and will continue until the position(s) are filled. Applicants will be notified if their application is being retained in the hiring pool for up to two years. Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Close Date Applications will be: Applications will be accepted and screened for the duration of this pool. Special Instructions This position is not eligible for new sponsorship. Review of applications will be on a continual basis and will continue until the position(s) are filled. Applicants are retained in the hiring pool for up to two years. EEO Statement Montana State University is an equal opportunity employer. MSU does not discriminate against any applicant on the basis of race, color, religion, creed, political ideas, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, marital status, national origin, physical or mental disability, or any other protected class status in violation of any applicable law. In compliance with the Montana Veteran’s Employment Preference Act, MSU provides preference in employment to veterans, disabled veterans, and certain eligible relatives of veterans. To claim veteran’s preference, please complete the veteran’s preference information located in the Demographics section of your profile. FLSA Details FLSA Determination FLSA Status Exempt Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Resume OR Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). University Human Resources 920 Technology BLVD, Suite A Bozeman, MT 59718 406-994-3651 humanresources@montana.edu Accessibility | Contact List | Directories | Jobs | Legal & Privacy Policy | Site Index Montana State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/53335": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Architecture",
      "description": "Montana State University Employment Opportunities | Assistant Professor of Architecture Skip to Main Content Jobs at Montana State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About MSU About Bozeman Benefits Academics Assistant Professor of Architecture Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Announcement Number FAC - VA - 27026 For questions regarding this position, please contact: Brian Kelly brian.kelly4@montana.edu Classification Title Working Title Assistant Professor of Architecture Brief Position Overview Faculty Tenure Track No Faculty Rank Assistant Professor Position Number 4A4420 & 4A5219 Department Architecture Division College of Arts & Architecture Appointment Type Faculty Contract Term Academic Year Semester If other, specify From date If other, specify End date Union Affiliation Exempt from Collective Bargaining FTE 1.0 Benefits Eligible Eligible Salary Salary commensurate with experience, education, and qualifications. Contract Type MUS If other, please specify Recruitment Type Open Position Details General Statement We seek faculty to foster innovation in applied design research for the built environment. Candidates are expected to have the ability to teach architectural design studios throughout the curriculum and have a specialty in at least one of the following areas: building construction; computation and digital technology; environmental systems; or structures. Candidates must have the ability to advance teaching and research in innovative design that integrates social, environmental, and technical considerations. Candidates will be expected to develop and maintain an active program of scholarly and creative work within the discipline. Duties and Responsibilities We hope to attract applicants who can teach effectively to the University community and have demonstrated ability in helping students from varying backgrounds to succeed. Teach on-campus in person. Advise, evaluate, and assist students. Innovative curriculum and/or course development. Participate in faculty meetings and service assignments. Meet regularly with, collaborating with, and supporting multi-section teaching and learning objectives Required Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills Candidates must have a terminal degree of a Master of Architecture or greater. In exceptional circumstances, the education and experience prerequisites may be exempted where the candidate can demonstrate an equivalent combination of education and experience relevant to the appointment. Preferred Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills 1. Professional architectural licensure ( NCARB recognized) 2. Three or more years of professional teaching experience in higher education 3. Expertise in architectural design as demonstrated through submitted materials 4. Scholarship in the field of design 5. The ability to teach design studio (at various levels), lecture, and seminar courses in identified focus areas The Successful Candidate Will Engage with undergraduate and graduate students while providing mentorship to a varying student body. Have effective interpersonal skills including the ability to collaborate successfully with faculty and staff. Possess excellent written, graphic, and oral communication skills. Be skilled in utilizing innovative pedagogy that engages students in the learning process. Have the potential to provide leadership and to assume responsibility for organizational and program activities. Position Special Requirements/Additional Information This job description should not be construed as an exhaustive statement of duties, responsibilities or requirements, but a general description of the job. Nothing contained herein restricts Montana State University’s rights to assign or reassign duties and responsibilities to this job at any time. Physical Demands To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. The requirements listed above are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. The Program As a land-grant institution located in the heart of the Greater Yellowstone ecosystem and the Rocky Mountains, the School of Architecture and Montana State University are internationally recognized for research and creative activity drawn from the social, cultural, and environmental conditions of the western landscape. The School of Architecture offers a four-year pre-professional undergraduate program leading to a one-and-a-half year professional Master of Architecture degree fully accredited by the National Architectural Accrediting Board ( NAAB ). The program has approximately 400 undergraduate and 80 graduate students. In addition, the school has a strong connection with alumni to help students transition into the profession. https://arch.montana.edu We believe in broad engagement with the cultural and ecological context through architecture’s agency in the world. The School of Architecture empowers students to engage the complexities of social and ecological systems through creative, collaborative and ethical design of the built environment. We instill personal agency, self-reflection and environmental empathy to educate innovators who challenge and advance the design professions. The Department The College The College of Arts & Architecture is home to distinctive academic programs within the Schools of Art, Architecture, Music and Film & Photography. Students enjoy close mentoring relationships with faculty through a curriculum that is rich in studio- and lab-based pedagogies. The College offers international and cultural travel opportunities for students in all majors and encourages internship experiences for many of its programs. The College hosts the only accredited architecture program in Montana and supports a unique, world-class graduate program in science and natural history filmmaking. Graduates from the college enjoy successful careers in art, design, media production, photography, architecture, education, and music. They also apply the discipline-specific, creative problem-solving skills and work ethic established in their programs to career opportunities in areas outside the arts. The College is home to the internationally recognized Montana Shakespeare in the Parks and supports the Black Box Theatre as well as innovation and design spaces including the Design Sandbox for Engaged Learning ( DSEL ) and the Community Design Center ( CDC ). For more information about the College of Arts and Architecture, visit our website: www.montana.edu/caa Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 2 Desired Start Date August 2027 Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Close Date Applications will be: Screening of applications will begin on November 16, 2026 ; however, applications will continue to be accepted until an adequate applicant pool has been established. Special Instructions EEO Statement Montana State University is an equal opportunity employer. MSU does not discriminate against any applicant on the basis of race, color, religion, creed, political ideas, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, marital status, national origin, physical or mental disability, or any other protected class status in violation of any applicable law. In compliance with the Montana Veteran’s Employment Preference Act, MSU provides preference in employment to veterans, disabled veterans, and certain eligible relatives of veterans. To claim veteran’s preference, please complete the veteran’s preference information located in the Demographics section of your profile. FLSA Details FLSA Determination FLSA Status Exempt Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Teaching Statement (max 2 pages) Research Statement Portfolio - Research, Professional Practices &/or Teaching (max 20 pages) Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). University Human Resources 920 Technology BLVD, Suite A Bozeman, MT 59718 406-994-3651 humanresources@montana.edu Accessibility | Contact List | Directories | Jobs | Legal & Privacy Policy | Site Index Montana State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/53315": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Structural Biology or Quantum Biochemistry",
      "description": "Montana State University Employment Opportunities | Assistant Professor of Structural Biology or Quantum Biochemistry Skip to Main Content Jobs at Montana State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About MSU About Bozeman Benefits Academics Assistant Professor of Structural Biology or Quantum Biochemistry Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. As part of your application, please upload the following required documents: Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter addressing the Required and Preferred Qualifications Research Statement (maximum 4 pages) Teaching Statement (maximum 3 pages) Letters of Recommendation and Reference Calls: All applicants will be required to provide a minimum of three references during the application process. After initial screenings, references for top applicants will be contacted by email to request a letter of recommendation, due within one week of email notification (please notify your references in advance). References for finalist(s) will also be contacted by phone during the finalist stage. Position Details Position Information Announcement Number FAC - VA - 27014 For questions regarding this position, please contact: Kimberly Hilmer Business Operations Manager kimberly.hilmer@montana.edu Classification Title Working Title Assistant Professor of Structural Biology or Quantum Biochemistry Brief Position Overview The Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry at Montana State University invites applications for two tenure-track faculty positions in biochemistry (structural biology and quantum biochemistry) Faculty Tenure Track Yes Faculty Rank Assistant Professor Position Number 4A3167 and 4A4086 Department Chemistry Division College of Letters & Science Appointment Type Faculty Contract Term Academic Year Semester If other, specify From date If other, specify End date Union Affiliation Exempt from Collective Bargaining FTE 1.0 Benefits Eligible Eligible Salary Salary commensurate with experience, education, and qualifications Contract Type MUS If other, please specify Recruitment Type Open Position Details General Statement The Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry at Montana State University invites applications for two tenure-track faculty positions in biochemistry. The first position is for applicants with interest and expertise in structural biology who will leverage the department’s state-of-the-art NMR , Cryo-EM or mass spectrometry facilities to advance their research goals. The second position in quantum biochemistry is for applicants who seek to advance, elucidate, and exploit quantum effects in biological processes such as photochemistry, magnetic sensing, electron and proton transport, biocatalysis, or other research fields associated with molecular biophysics. Research programs that take advantage of innovative new approaches for probing nuclear or electronic spin states to provide new biochemical insight are also of interest. Applicants should indicate in their cover letter the position to which they are applying. Appointments will be considered at the Assistant Professor level, although appointments at the Associate Professor level will be possible in exceptional circumstances. Duties and Responsibilities As a tenure-track faculty member in the Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry, the successful candidate will conduct research activities in Biochemistry and establish an independent, productive, externally funded, nationally competitive research program. Duties also include teaching at the undergraduate and graduate levels in areas of chemistry that are of mutual interest to the Department and the candidate, advising and mentoring undergraduate and graduate students, participating in appropriate departmental and university service functions, and collaborating with other faculty and departments to enhance scholarship and pedagogy at Montana State University. We hope to attract applicants who can teach in a university community and have demonstrated ability in helping students from all backgrounds to succeed. Required Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills Ph.D. in Chemistry or a related area by start date. Potential to establish an internationally recognized and externally funded independent research program. Potential to effectively teach and mentor undergraduate and graduate students. Preferred Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills Postdoctoral experience. Interest in and ability to establish multidisciplinary collaborative research. Demonstrated excellence in undergraduate and graduate teaching and research. The Successful Candidate Will Be a dynamic, committed, and visionary scientist and educator who will advance MSU’s goals of outstanding research, teaching, and service. Have excellent communication skills. Have an appreciation for all constituencies and continuously support, promote, and build a whole community that includes people of all backgrounds. Position Special Requirements/Additional Information To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. The requirements listed above are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. Physical Demands To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. The requirements listed above are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. The Program The Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry is one of Montana State University’s premier departments. We continually strive for excellence in all of MSU’s core values. We are a vibrant, cohesive community with faculty, staff, and students who are dedicated to teaching, research, and service. The department has identified three primary areas of research emphasis. These three themes are energy conversion, supramolecular/mesoscale materials, and research at the chemistry/biology interface. The Department is uniquely positioned to perform energy conversion research across a wide range of material substrates using highly sophisticated instrumentation and methods. We are also well placed to perform supramolecular/mesoscale research on a breadth of sample types including synthetic materials, protein networks, and viruses. Finally, we are able to provide new chemical insights into biology using a vast array of methods that have been developed or enhanced within the Department. Fundamental research programs in additional areas of chemistry and biochemistry are also important for the development of these research themes. State-of-the-art instrumentation and shared instrumentation facilities are essential infrastructure for all of the research themes. Our Department is a University Flagship, and our faculty members play leading roles in multi-disciplinary research programs that integrate efforts across the College of Letters and Science, across Montana State University, and with other academic institutions and industrial partners both locally and more widely. We leverage our research activities to provide outstanding opportunities for our students, post-doctoral associates, and staff scientists. After earning their degrees, our Ph.D. graduates have taken positions in universities, industry, and government labs. These graduates are highly sought after because of their excellent training and demonstrated records of accomplishment. As an integral part of our scientific lives, we are committed to excellence in training the next generation of scientists. Our faculty, staff, and students share a common vision of maintaining a collegial environment in which the professional, intellectual, and personal growth of each individual is nurtured. We strive to stimulate all of our students to learn, to imagine, and to discover. We strive to equip them with every tool that they need to flourish in their own exciting and rewarding careers. The Department The Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry at Montana State University ( MSU ) is a vigorous, research-active department with strong interdisciplinary collaborations. Research thrusts of the Department and University include structural biology, biophysics, bioinorganic chemistry, organic chemistry, physical chemistry, nanomaterials, optical spectroscopy, and energy research. The Department is composed of 17 tenure-track faculty, several research faculty and approximately 90 graduate students. The Department grants Ph.D. degrees in both Chemistry and Biochemistry and also has a strong tradition of undergraduate participation in research. The Department’s research building (built in 2008) houses shared instrumentation including a new macromolecular X-ray diffractometer, NMR and Mass spectrometry facilities, high-field and pulsed EPR , CD, femtosecond laser spectrometers, microscopes, FTIR spectrometers, steady-state and time-resolved emission laser spectrometers, molecular graphics, and parallel computing with a 90-processor heterogeneous Linux cluster. We have also recently installed a cryo-electron microscope, the only instrument of its kind within the greater 5-state, Northern Plains and Northern Rockies region. Other instruments, including SEM , TEM , confocal microscopy, scanning Auger, and scanning probe techniques, are available in shared user facilities at MSU . MSU is connected to the very broadband network system (vBNS) that provides fast Internet access and facilitates remote computing at national supercomputer sites. The College The College of Letters and Science ( CLS ), the largest center for learning, teaching and research at Montana State University, offers students an excellent liberal arts and sciences education in nearly 50 majors, 25 minors and over 25 graduate degrees within the four areas of the humanities, social sciences, natural and physical sciences, and mathematical sciences. Building on the great strength of our traditional disciplines, the college provides exciting opportunities for faculty and students at the cutting edge of interdisciplinary inquiry. CLS is dedicated to supporting student success, discovering and disseminating new knowledge, and providing an atmosphere in which discovery and learning are integrated and valued. CLS is at the confluence of intellectual tradition, discovery, and innovation. Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 2 Desired Start Date August 2027 Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Close Date Applications will be: Screening of applications will begin on October 23, 2026 ; however, applications will continue to be accepted until an adequate applicant pool has been established. Special Instructions As part of your application, please upload the following required documents: Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter addressing the Required and Preferred Qualifications Research Statement (maximum 4 pages) Teaching Statement (maximum 3 pages) Letters of Recommendation and Reference Calls: All applicants will be required to provide a minimum of three references during the application process. After initial screenings, references for top applicants will be contacted by email to request a letter of recommendation, due within one week of email notification (please notify your references in advance). References for finalist(s) will also be contacted by phone during the finalist stage. EEO Statement Montana State University is an equal opportunity employer. MSU does not discriminate against any applicant on the basis of race, color, religion, creed, political ideas, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, marital status, national origin, physical or mental disability, or any other protected class status in violation of any applicable law. In compliance with the Montana Veteran’s Employment Preference Act, MSU provides preference in employment to veterans, disabled veterans, and certain eligible relatives of veterans. To claim veteran’s preference, please complete the veteran’s preference information located in the Demographics section of your profile. FLSA Details FLSA Determination FLSA Status Exempt Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter addressing each of the Required and Preferred Qualifications Research Statement Teaching Statement Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). University Human Resources 920 Technology BLVD, Suite A Bozeman, MT 59718 406-994-3651 humanresources@montana.edu Accessibility | Contact List | Directories | Jobs | Legal & Privacy Policy | Site Index Montana State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/53308": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of American Studies",
      "description": "Montana State University Employment Opportunities | Assistant Professor of American Studies Skip to Main Content Jobs at Montana State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About MSU About Bozeman Benefits Academics Assistant Professor of American Studies Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. As part of your application, please upload the following required documents: Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter addressing each of the Required and Preferred Qualifications Research Statement (max 2 pages) Teaching Statement (max 2 pages) Letters of Recommendation and Reference Calls : All applicants will be required to provide a minimum of three references during the application process. Upon submission of the application, references will be contacted automatically by email to request a letter of recommendation, due by the screening date (please notify your references in advance). References for finalist(s) will also be contacted by phone during the finalist stage. Position Details Position Information Announcement Number FAC - VA - 27025 For questions regarding this position, please contact: William G. Thomas III Dean College of Letters & Science william.thomas22@montana.edu Classification Title Working Title Assistant Professor of American Studies Brief Position Overview The College of Letters & Science at Montana State University seeks to hire a tenure-track assistant professor specializing in American Studies beginning August 15, 2027. Faculty Tenure Track Yes Faculty Rank Assistant Professor Position Number 4A0622 Department American Studies Division College of Letters & Science Appointment Type Faculty Contract Term Academic Year Semester If other, specify From date If other, specify End date Union Affiliation Exempt from Collective Bargaining FTE 1.0 Benefits Eligible Eligible Salary Salary commensurate with experience, education, and qualifications Contract Type MUS If other, please specify Recruitment Type Open Position Details General Statement The American Studies Program at Montana State University ( MSU ), Bozeman, seeks to hire an assistant professor with the ability to work professionally and effectively with individuals from all backgrounds, possess effective interpersonal, written and verbal communication skills and has the ability to contribute positively to the academic success of the students and the land-grant mission of Montana State University. Candidates must demonstrate a record of scholarship and training in American Studies or a relevant field, an interdisciplinary research program, and the potential to be an outstanding and effective teacher at the undergraduate and graduate levels. We are especially interested in candidates with expertise in place-based studies, environmental humanities, historical geography, western American studies, or related fields. Duties and Responsibilities This position will be a full-time, tenure-track appointment with primary responsibilities in research and teaching at the undergraduate and graduate levels in American Studies, as well as in the department in which tenure will reside. The successful candidate will be expected to engage in outreach and service in the state of Montana and the broader community. The teaching load will be consistent with faculty in the department where tenure resides. Required Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills Ph.D. in American Studies or a related field by start date. Demonstrated potential for excellence in both teaching and scholarship. Teaching record demonstrating the ability to offer courses in American Studies or a related field at the graduate and undergraduate levels. Preferred Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills Potential to conduct research and teach in critical theory and research methods. Successful record of fellowships or grants, or experience with externally funded research. Interest and ability to contribute to the College’s programs and expertise in place-based studies, such as environmental humanities, historical geography, western American studies, or related fields. The Successful Candidate Will Be a dynamic teacher and scholar. Have the ability to inspire and mentor students. Have excellent written and oral communication skills. Be committed to supporting, promoting, and building a whole community, which includes people of many backgrounds, through research, teaching, and service. Position Special Requirements/Additional Information This job description should not be construed as an exhaustive statement of duties, responsibilities or requirements, but a general description of the job. Nothing contained herein restricts Montana State University’s rights to assign or reassign duties and responsibilities to this job at any time. Physical Demands To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. The requirements listed above are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. The Program The American Studies Program at Montana State University is an interdisciplinary doctoral and master’s graduate degree program which also offers undergraduate courses and electives. The program provides students with a deep understanding of the history, literature, arts, politics, regions and identities of North America and the U.S. The program emphasizes the complexity and variation in the experience of American lives and prepares students to help address the important and profound questions of the world today. The program connects students with interdisciplinary research centers, such as the Ivan Doig Center for the Study of the Lands and Peoples of the North American West; the Geospatial Core Facility; the Interdisciplinary Institute on Artificial Intelligence; and the Center for Science, Technology, Ethics and Society. The Department The College The College of Letters and Science ( CLS ), the largest center for learning, teaching and research at Montana State University, offers students an excellent liberal arts and sciences education in nearly 50 majors, 25 minors and over 25 graduate degrees within the four areas of the humanities, social sciences, natural and physical sciences, and mathematical sciences. Building on the great strength of our traditional disciplines, the college provides exciting opportunities for faculty and students at the cutting edge of interdisciplinary inquiry. CLS is dedicated to supporting student success, discovering and disseminating new knowledge, and providing an atmosphere in which discovery and learning are integrated and valued. CLS is at the confluence of intellectual tradition, discovery, and innovation. Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date Upon completion of a successful search. Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Close Date Applications will be: Screening of applications will begin on November 19, 2026 ; however, applications will continue to be accepted until an adequate applicant pool has been established. Special Instructions As part of your application, please upload the following required documents: Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter addressing each of the Required and Preferred Qualifications Research Statement (max 2 pages) Teaching Statement (max 2 pages) Letters of Recommendation and Reference Calls : All applicants will be required to provide a minimum of three references during the application process. Upon submission of the application, references will be contacted automatically by email to request a letter of recommendation, due by the screening date (please notify your references in advance). References for finalist(s) will also be contacted by phone during the finalist stage. EEO Statement Montana State University is an equal opportunity employer. MSU does not discriminate against any applicant on the basis of race, color, religion, creed, political ideas, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, marital status, national origin, physical or mental disability, or any other protected class status in violation of any applicable law. In compliance with the Montana Veteran’s Employment Preference Act, MSU provides preference in employment to veterans, disabled veterans, and certain eligible relatives of veterans. To claim veteran’s preference, please complete the veteran’s preference information located in the Demographics section of your profile. FLSA Details FLSA Determination FLSA Status Exempt Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter addressing each of the Required and Preferred Qualifications Research Statement Teaching Statement Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). University Human Resources 920 Technology BLVD, Suite A Bozeman, MT 59718 406-994-3651 humanresources@montana.edu Accessibility | Contact List | Directories | Jobs | Legal & Privacy Policy | Site Index Montana State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/53306": {
      "title": "Agronomic Entomologist",
      "description": "Montana State University Employment Opportunities | Agronomic Entomologist Skip to Main Content Jobs at Montana State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About MSU About Bozeman Benefits Academics Agronomic Entomologist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Announcement Number FAC - VA - 27009 For questions regarding this position, please contact: Michael Ivie mivie@montana.edu 406-994-4610 Classification Title Working Title Agronomic Entomologist Brief Position Overview Montana State University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Agronomic Entomology in the Department of Plant Sciences and Plant Pathology. The successful candidate will develop an innovative, externally funded research program addressing fundamental and applied questions in the biology, ecology, and management of insects in agricultural systems. The position offers opportunities to collaborate across a diverse community of agricultural and biological scientists and to engage with Montana’s agricultural stakeholders. Teaching will contribute to our growing entomology programs, including courses such as Integrated Pest Management and Insect Physiology. Faculty Tenure Track Yes Faculty Rank Assistant Professor Position Number 4A3187 Department Plant Sciences Division College of Agriculture/MAES Appointment Type Faculty Contract Term Academic Year Semester If other, specify From date If other, specify End date Union Affiliation Exempt from Collective Bargaining FTE 1.0 Benefits Eligible Eligible Salary Salary commensurate with experience, education, and qualifications Contract Type MUS If other, please specify Recruitment Type Open Position Details General Statement The Department of Plant Sciences and Plant Pathology seeks a talented and collaborative colleague who will develop an innovative research program in agronomic entomology. The successful candidate will contribute to and collaborate across departmental and college strengths in cropping systems, plant health, integrated pest management, agroecology, plant-insect interactions, entomology, weed science, plant breeding and genetics, precision agriculture, and sustainable agricultural systems. Montana provides exceptional opportunities to address applied and fundamental questions related to the ecology and management of insect pests in dryland and irrigated cropping systems, including cereal, pulse, oilseed, forage, and specialty crops. We welcome candidates using diverse field, laboratory, molecular, physiological, and/or systems-based approaches to address important insect-management challenges in agricultural systems. This is a nine-month (academic year), tenure-track faculty position at the Assistant Professor level with research (60%), teaching (30%), and service (10%) responsibilities funded by the Montana Agricultural Experiment Station and the College of Agriculture. Duties and Responsibilities Research responsibilities include developing a nationally recognized, externally funded program in agronomic entomology that addresses applied and fundamental questions relevant to Montana and the broader region. Research should address the biology, ecology, and management of economically important insect pests in agricultural systems and may incorporate beneficial insects and their roles in agroecosystems. Montana provides exceptional opportunities to address arthropod challenges in dryland and irrigated cropping systems, including wheat stem sawfly and other insect pests affecting cereal, pulse, oilseed, forage, specialty crop, and horticultural production systems. Candidates may employ diverse approaches, including integrated pest management, plant-insect interactions, insect physiology, landscape ecology, molecular approaches, or related disciplines. The successful candidate will establish a Montana Agricultural Experiment Station Hatch Project, secure extramural funding, publish research in appropriate scholarly outlets, and mentor graduate and undergraduate researchers. This position may have opportunities for travel to off-campus sites. Teaching responsibilities include the upper-division undergraduate course Integrated Pest Management ( AGSC 401) and the graduate course Insect Physiology ( ENTO 520), along with other courses appropriate to the candidate’s expertise and programmatic needs. The successful candidate will contribute to the Entomology Minor and MS in Entomology programs and participate in undergraduate and graduate student advising and mentoring. Service responsibilities include active participation in departmental, college, and university service as appropriate to career stage and programmatic needs; engagement with agricultural stakeholders and other communities consistent with the missions of a Land-Grant University and the Montana Agricultural Experiment Station; and participation in relevant professional organizations. Required Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills Ph.D. in entomology or an appropriate related field at time of appointment. Academic or professional training in agronomic entomology in agricultural systems. Demonstrated potential for excellence in research in agronomic entomology. Demonstrated experience or potential for effective interdisciplinary collaboration addressing agricultural issues. Demonstrated potential for excellence in undergraduate and graduate instruction and mentoring. Preferred Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills Demonstrated ability or strong potential to secure extramural funding. Evidence of excellence in research relevant to agronomic entomology. Demonstrated excellence in undergraduate and/or graduate instruction and mentoring. Demonstrated ability or strong potential to engage effectively with agricultural producers, industry, agencies, and/or other stakeholders to address management challenges. Demonstrated ability to collaborate across academic disciplines and with internal and external partners. Demonstrated ability or potential to effectively mentor students from many backgrounds. The Successful Candidate Will Possess excellent written and oral communication skills. Possess effective interpersonal skills and the ability to develop positive working relationships with faculty, staff, students, agricultural producers, and other external stakeholders. Demonstrate initiative, adaptability, and the ability to work effectively both independently and as a member of interdisciplinary teams. Demonstrate the ability to work effectively with students and colleagues from many backgrounds. Position Special Requirements/Additional Information Must possess a valid driver’s license, an acceptable driving record, and meet all State of Montana requirements to operate State/University vehicles. (If successful candidate possesses a valid out-of-state driver’s license, must obtain a valid Montana driver’s license within 60 days of hire.) This job description should not be construed as an exhaustive statement of duties, responsibilities or requirements, but a general description of the job. Nothing contained herein restricts Montana State University’s rights to assign or reassign duties and responsibilities to this job at any time. Physical Demands To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. The requirements listed above are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. The Program The Department The College Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date Upon completion of a successful search. Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Close Date Applications will be: Screening of applications will begin on October 15, 2026 ; however, applications will continue to be accepted until an adequate applicant pool has been established. Special Instructions EEO Statement Montana State University is an equal opportunity employer. MSU does not discriminate against any applicant on the basis of race, color, religion, creed, political ideas, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, marital status, national origin, physical or mental disability, or any other protected class status in violation of any applicable law. In compliance with the Montana Veteran’s Employment Preference Act, MSU provides preference in employment to veterans, disabled veterans, and certain eligible relatives of veterans. To claim veteran’s preference, please complete the veteran’s preference information located in the Demographics section of your profile. FLSA Details FLSA Determination FLSA Status Exempt Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Research Statement List of Three (3) Professional References Teaching Statement Cover Letter addressing each of the Required and Preferred Qualifications Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). University Human Resources 920 Technology BLVD, Suite A Bozeman, MT 59718 406-994-3651 humanresources@montana.edu Accessibility | Contact List | Directories | Jobs | Legal & Privacy Policy | Site Index Montana State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/53277": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Computer Science",
      "description": "Montana State University Employment Opportunities | Assistant Professor of Computer Science Skip to Main Content Jobs at Montana State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About MSU About Bozeman Benefits Academics Assistant Professor of Computer Science Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Required Documents to be uploaded: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Brief Research Statement (2 page maximum) Brief Teaching Statement (2 page maximum) Two (2) Publications Position Details Position Information Announcement Number FAC - VA - 27008 For questions regarding this position, please contact: Denise Palmquist 406-994-4780 denise.palmquist@montana.edu Classification Title Working Title Assistant Professor of Computer Science Brief Position Overview The Gianforte School of Computing invites applications for multiple full-time tenure-track positions at the level of Assistant Professor. Primary responsibilities include developing a nationally recognized, externally funded research program, teaching both undergraduate and graduate courses consistent with the candidate’s background, and participating in professional/service activities. Faculty Tenure Track Yes Faculty Rank Assistant Position Number 4A3170 and 4A3312 Department Gianforte School of Computing Division College of Engineering Appointment Type Faculty Contract Term Academic Year Semester Fall or Spring If other, specify From date If other, specify End date Union Affiliation Exempt from Collective Bargaining FTE 1.0 Benefits Eligible Eligible Salary Salary commensurate with experience, education, and qualifications Contract Type MUS If other, please specify Recruitment Type Open Position Details General Statement The Gianforte School of Computing, housed in the Norm Asbjornson College of Engineering ( NACOE ) at Montana State University, invites applications for multiple full-time tenure-track positions at the level of Assistant Professor. Duties include developing a nationally recognized, externally funded research program, teaching, developing courses, mentoring and service. Applications are encouraged from candidates with expertise in all areas of computer science. Duties and Responsibilities Develop a nationally recognized, externally funded research program; produce scholarly works; contribute to School of Computing undergraduate and graduate instruction, mentor and advise; and participate in professional/service/outreach activities. Required Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills Ph.D. in Computer Science or a related field upon start date. Potential to build a nationally recognized, externally funded research program. Evidence of scholarly and professional achievements commensurate with experience. Preferred Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills Research and teaching expertise that enhances our organization’s capabilities and strengths, especially in areas such as artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, data science, machine learning, quantum and/or systems. We also encourage applications from candidates whose research and teaching expertise complement existing expertise. Ability to work with and engage a broad range of students and colleagues within and outside the School of Computing. The Successful Candidate Will Be a dynamic researcher and communicator who has: excellent written and oral communication skills; the ability to inspire and mentor students; the ability to establish a funded research program; the potential to teach and collaborate effectively in a University community; the ability to help students with varying backgrounds succeed; and effective interpersonal skills. Position Special Requirements/Additional Information This job description should not be construed as an exhaustive statement of duties, responsibilities, or requirements, but a general description of the job. Nothing contained herein restricts Montana State University’s rights to assign or reassign duties and responsibilities to this job at any time. Physical Demands To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. The requirements listed above are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. The Program The Department The Gianforte School of Computing (GSoC) at Montana State University supports the mission of the Norm Asbjornson College of Engineering and the University through its teaching, research, and service activities. The GSoC serves approximately 400 majors, 100 minors and 70 graduate students by preparing them for computing careers and for a lifetime of learning. The GSoC offers a broad array of curricular opportunities in computing areas that include Computer Science (minor, B.S. degree, B.A. degree, M.S. degree, Ph.D. degree), Data Science (minor, B.S. degree) and Cybersecurity (M.S. degree). The GSoC is the anchor occupant of a beautiful, mass timber building that opens in Fall 2026 and contains desirable spaces that facilitate high quality research, instruction and outreach. The College The Norm Asbjornson College of Engineering comprises five academic departments (Chemical & Biological Engineering, Civil Engineering, Gianforte School of Computing, Electrical & Computer Engineering, and Mechanical & Industrial Engineering) and is home to numerous research centers such as the Center for Biofilm Engineering and the Western Transportation Institute. The College enrolls approximately 3,100 undergraduate students and 250 graduate students. Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 2 Desired Start Date Upon a successful search Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Close Date Applications will be: S creening of applications will begin on November 16th 2026; however, applications will continue to be accepted until an adequate applicant pool has been established. Special Instructions Required Documents to be uploaded: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Brief Research Statement (2 page maximum) Brief Teaching Statement (2 page maximum) Two (2) Publications EEO Statement Montana State University is an equal opportunity employer. MSU does not discriminate against any applicant on the basis of race, color, religion, creed, political ideas, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, marital status, national origin, physical or mental disability, or any other protected class status in violation of any applicable law. In compliance with the Montana Veteran’s Employment Preference Act, MSU provides preference in employment to veterans, disabled veterans, and certain eligible relatives of veterans. To claim veteran’s preference, please complete the veteran’s preference information located in the Demographics section of your profile. FLSA Details FLSA Determination FLSA Status Exempt Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Teaching Statement (max 2 pages) Research Statement Other #2 - Please see Special Instructions Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). University Human Resources 920 Technology BLVD, Suite A Bozeman, MT 59718 406-994-3651 humanresources@montana.edu Accessibility | Contact List | Directories | Jobs | Legal & Privacy Policy | Site Index Montana State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/53258": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Film Production",
      "description": "Montana State University Employment Opportunities | Assistant Professor of Film Production Skip to Main Content Jobs at Montana State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About MSU About Bozeman Benefits Academics Assistant Professor of Film Production Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Announcement Number FAC - VA - 27024 For questions regarding this position, please contact: Shelley Fleming 406-994-6224 rochelle.fleming@montana.edu Classification Title Working Title Assistant Professor of Film Production Brief Position Overview The School of Film & Photography at Montana State University-Bozeman invites applications for a full-time, tenure-eligible Assistant Professor of Film beginning August 2027. We seek a colleague with the knowledge to teach production courses in the School’s undergraduate and graduate film curriculum with a focus on fiction film production. The proposed tenure-track faculty position will be a key contributor to our film undergraduate program and our award-winning M.F.A in Science and Natural History Filmmaking. The candidate is expected to teach in our core BA Film and BFA in Integrated Lens-based Media programs, develop and maintain an active creative research agenda, and participate in service responsibilities. Faculty Tenure Track Yes Faculty Rank Assistant Professor Position Number 4A3139 Department School of Film and Photography Division College of Arts & Architecture Appointment Type Faculty Contract Term Academic Year Semester If other, specify From date If other, specify End date Union Affiliation Exempt from Collective Bargaining FTE 1.0 Benefits Eligible Eligible Salary Salary commensurate with experience, education, and qualifications. Contract Type MUS If other, please specify Recruitment Type Open Position Details General Statement The School of Film & Photography at Montana State University-Bozeman invites applications for a full-time, tenure-eligible Assistant Professor of Film Production beginning August 2027. We aim to find a colleague whose creative work transcends traditional boundaries between film and related media with the ability to teach subjects across the school’s undergraduate and graduate filmmaking curriculum. Montana State University values diverse perspectives and is committed to continually supporting, promoting, and building an inclusive and culturally diverse campus environment. In addition, M.S.U. recognizes the importance of work-life integration and strives to be responsive to the needs of dual-career couples. Duties and Responsibilities Develop and maintain a creative research agenda and record of accomplishment Demonstrate teaching effectiveness and participate in program development and assessment Advise undergraduate students and serve on MFA graduate committees Participate in curriculum development and assessment Contribute to recruitment, retention, and outreach activities Participate in School, College, and University committees Required Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills MFA or other terminal degree in Film, Media Production, or related fields Active filmmaking agenda with a distinguished public record of original creative works and/or comparable professional work in narrative filmmaking Experience in college-level teaching Ability to teach comprehensive fiction production courses in the undergraduate program Ability to teach film production across all levels Ability to teach specialty courses in directing, cinematography, and lighting Openness to teaching and mentoring students in an array of filmmaking styles and voices Ability to teach in a university community and support the success of students from varying backgrounds Preferred Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills Owing to the breadth and integration of our programs, candidates who demonstrate experience, education, knowledge & additional interest, and expertise in one or more of the following areas will be given preference: Ability to teach nonfiction production courses at the undergraduate level and in our MFA Science and Natural History Program Experience working on-set or additional relevant production skills and field of experience The Successful Candidate Will Be able to work closely with other faculty in a collegiate environment and contribute to the school’s academic mission. Demonstrate openness to differing perspectives and contribute to a dynamic intellectual environment within the department. Position Special Requirements/Additional Information This job description should not be construed as an exhaustive statement of duties, responsibilities, or requirements, but a general description of the job. Nothing contained herein restricts Montana State University’s rights to assign or reassign duties and responsibilities to this job at any time. Physical Demands To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. The requirements listed above are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. The Program The School of Film and Photography ( SFP ) offers B.A. programs in film and photography options, a B.F.A. in integrated Lens-Based Media, and an M.F.A. program in Science and Natural History Filmmaking. The Department The School of Film and Photography ( SFP ) is part of the College of Arts and Architecture, including the School of Architecture, School of Art, and the School of Music. SFP represents faculty and students engaged in creating and analyzing film, video, photography, and theatre. The School serves 219 film & video production majors with a unique curriculum that combines film and video production with theatre and critical studies; 84 photography majors with a curriculum that includes traditional, digital, and alternative processes; 43 B.F.A. students in our Integrated Lens-Based Media major representing a fusion of our film and photography curriculums, and 35 M.F.A. candidates in a documentary film and video production program that emphasizes science and natural history filmmaking. Faculty research interests span various creative disciplines: narrative, documentary, and experimental film production; digital, analog, and alternative process photography; film studies and critical theory; and theater production. The College The College of Arts and Architecture is home to distinctive academic programs housed in the Schools of Art, Architecture, Music, and Film & Photography. Students enjoy close mentoring relationships with faculty through a curriculum that is rich in-studio and lab-based pedagogy. The College offers international and cultural travel opportunities for students in all majors and encourages internship experiences for many of its programs. The College hosts the only accredited Architecture program in Montana and supports a unique, world-class graduate film program in Science and Natural History Filmmaking. Graduates from the College enjoy successful careers in art, design, media and film production, photography, architecture, education, and music as well as apply the discipline, creative problems solving skills and work ethic embedded in their programs to any career. The College is home to the internationally recognized Montana Shakespeare in the Parks theater company and supports the Black Box Theatre and innovation and design spaces such as the Design Sandbox for Engaged Learning and the Community Design Center. For more information about the College of Arts and Architecture, go to: https://www.montana.edu/caa Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date August 2027 Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Close Date Applications will be: Screening of applications will begin on November 9th, 2026 ; however, applications will continue to be accepted until an adequate applicant pool has been established. Special Instructions EEO Statement Montana State University is an equal opportunity employer. MSU does not discriminate against any applicant on the basis of race, color, religion, creed, political ideas, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, marital status, national origin, physical or mental disability, or any other protected class status in violation of any applicable law. In compliance with the Montana Veteran’s Employment Preference Act, MSU provides preference in employment to veterans, disabled veterans, and certain eligible relatives of veterans. To claim veteran’s preference, please complete the veteran’s preference information located in the Demographics section of your profile. FLSA Details FLSA Determination FLSA Status Exempt Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter addressing each of the Required and Preferred Qualifications Sample Syllabus Sample Syllabus #2 Sample Creative Work Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). University Human Resources 920 Technology BLVD, Suite A Bozeman, MT 59718 406-994-3651 humanresources@montana.edu Accessibility | Contact List | Directories | Jobs | Legal & Privacy Policy | Site Index Montana State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/53257": {
      "title": "Mellon Assistant Research Professor of Native American Studies",
      "description": "Montana State University Employment Opportunities | Mellon Assistant Research Professor of Native American Studies Skip to Main Content Jobs at Montana State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About MSU About Bozeman Benefits Academics Mellon Assistant Research Professor of Native American Studies Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. As part of your application, please upload the following required documents: Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter addressing the Required and Preferred Qualifications References and Letters of Recommendation: All applicants will be required to provide a minimum of three references during the application process. References will be contacted automatically by email once the application is submitted to request a letter of recommendation. Applicants should notify their references in advance and let them know that letters must be submitted by the screening date. References may also be contacted by phone as part of the final reference check process during the finalist stage. Position Details Position Information Announcement Number FAC - VA - 27011 For questions regarding this position, please contact: Katie Sutich Assistant to the Dean 406-994-3065 katie.sutich@montana.edu Classification Title Working Title Mellon Assistant Research Professor of Native American Studies Brief Position Overview The Department of Native American Studies at Montana State University seeks a specialist in Native American legal history. Faculty Tenure Track No Faculty Rank Non-Tenure Track Position Number 4B4438 Department Native American Studies Division College of Letters & Science Appointment Type Non-Tenure Track Contract Term Fiscal Year Semester If other, specify From date If other, specify End date Union Affiliation AFMSU FTE 1.0 Benefits Eligible Eligible Salary Starting at $70,000, commensurate with experience, education, and qualifications Contract Type LOA If other, please specify Recruitment Type Open Position Details General Statement The Mellon Assistant Research Professor of Native American Studies will conduct research on Native American legal history, including federal Indian law, Indigenous legal systems and epistemologies, and/or Indigenous governance and sovereignty, and teach in Native American Studies. The position supports a grant from the Mellon Foundation to build an open educational resource. Duties and Responsibilities Conduct independent research in Native American legal history, including federal Indian law, Indigenous legal systems and epistemologies, and/or Indigenous governance and sovereignty in support of the \"Equality Before the Law” Open Educational Resource; Teach one course in the Native American Studies curriculum each year; Participate actively in the Department of Native American Studies at MSU , advise students, and promote student success; Coordinate and share research, storytelling, and programs with community and tribal partners; Support the development of the OER and the Mellon grant in partnership with PI and Co-PIs at the University of Nebraska-Lincoln and MSU ; and Present research at the project’s graduate fellows’ program, conferences, and other community gatherings. Required Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills PhD in History, Native American Studies, or a relevant field, completed by August 14, 2027. Demonstrated record of good scholarship and training in Indigenous and Native American History. Teaching record supporting the ability to offer courses in Native American Studies, History, or a related field at the graduate and undergraduate levels. Preferred Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills Demonstrated experience in research, teaching, and curricular development in Native American Studies or legal history. Demonstrated expertise in digital history, and/or community engaged partnerships. The Successful Candidate Will Possess excellent communication and interpersonal skills. Be able to work productively in a dynamic and interdisciplinary department. Be an effective advocate for the Department within the University and with external constituencies. Position Special Requirements/Additional Information This position is contingent upon continued grant funding. Funding is currently anticipated for two years, with the potential for additional funding. This job description should not be construed as an exhaustive statement of duties, responsibilities or requirements, but a general description of the job. Nothing contained herein restricts Montana State University’s rights to assign or reassign duties and responsibilities to this job at any time. Physical Demands To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodation. The requirements listed above are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. The Program The Department The Department of Native American Studies is in the College of Letters and Science. It is the only Indigenous Studies/Native American Studies program in a mainstream institution accredited by the World Indigenous Nations Higher Education Consortium ( WINHEC ). Uniquely, the NAS Department is home to the American Indian and Alaska Native Student Success Services ( AIANSSS ), providing wrap-around cultural programming and support to Indigenous students from all across campus (not just those enrolled in NAS academic programs). The Department offers a non-teaching undergraduate minor in Native American Studies ( NAS ), a graduate certificate in NAS and a Master of Arts in NAS . A new graduate certificate in Indigenous Food Systems has been approved and a new suite of courses to support this certificate are under development. Courses in Native American Studies are an integral part of the Diversity Category in the University Core requirements. Faculty teaching loads may include undergraduate and graduate courses. The Department of Native American Studies and its American Indian and Alaska Native Student Success Services are housed in American Indian Hall, a 32,000 square foot state-of-the-art office and classroom building opened in January of 2022. Faculty and staff in Native American Studies acknowledge and practice the Departmental core values of Honesty, Generosity, Kindness & Inclusivity, Hard Work, Family, Humility, Spirituality, Humor & Respect. We are guided by a Student Well-being Model developed collaboratively with our students, staff and faculty as part of the Department’s ongoing and successful work to earn and maintain accreditation with the World Indigenous Nations Higher Education Consortium ( WINHEC ). Integral to the Student Well-being Model are our Cultural Standards — Knowledge, Relationship, Land, Sovereignty— standards that we actively endeavor to weave through all the Department’s cultural, academic and administrative activities. The College The College of Letters and Science ( CLS ), the largest center for learning, teaching and research at Montana State University, offers students an excellent liberal arts and sciences education in nearly 50 majors, 25 minors and over 25 graduate degrees within the four areas of the humanities, social sciences, natural and physical sciences, and mathematics and social sciences. Building on the great strength of our traditional disciplines, the college provides exciting opportunities for faculty and students at the cutting edge of interdisciplinary inquiry. CLS is dedicated to supporting student success, discovering and disseminating new knowledge, and providing an atmosphere in which discovery and learning are integrated and valued. CLS is at the confluence of intellectual tradition, discovery, and innovation. Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date Upon completion of a successful search. Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Close Date Applications will be: Screening of applications will begin on November 3, 2026 ; however, applications will continue to be accepted until an adequate applicant pool has been established. Special Instructions As part of your application, please upload the following required documents: Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter addressing the Required and Preferred Qualifications References and Letters of Recommendation: All applicants will be required to provide a minimum of three references during the application process. References will be contacted automatically by email once the application is submitted to request a letter of recommendation. Applicants should notify their references in advance and let them know that letters must be submitted by the screening date. References may also be contacted by phone as part of the final reference check process during the finalist stage. EEO Statement Montana State University is an equal opportunity employer. MSU does not discriminate against any applicant on the basis of race, color, religion, creed, political ideas, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, marital status, national origin, physical or mental disability, or any other protected class status in violation of any applicable law. In compliance with the Montana Veteran’s Employment Preference Act, MSU provides preference in employment to veterans, disabled veterans, and certain eligible relatives of veterans. To claim veteran’s preference, please complete the veteran’s preference information located in the Demographics section of your profile. FLSA Details FLSA Determination FLSA Status Exempt Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). University Human Resources 920 Technology BLVD, Suite A Bozeman, MT 59718 406-994-3651 humanresources@montana.edu Accessibility | Contact List | Directories | Jobs | Legal & Privacy Policy | Site Index Montana State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/53244": {
      "title": "Finance Instructors for the Jake Jabs College of Business &amp; Entrepreneurship Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool)",
      "description": "Montana State University Employment Opportunities | Finance Instructors for the Jake Jabs College of Business &amp; Entrepreneurship Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) Skip to Main Content Jobs at Montana State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About MSU About Bozeman Benefits Academics Finance Instructors for the Jake Jabs College of Business & Entrepreneurship Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Documents required: A letter of application that includes (1) why you are interested in teaching in the finance option in the Jake Jabs College of Business & Entrepreneurship, and (2) what classes/finance topics you are most qualified to teach. A copy of the graduate-level academic transcript (unofficial transcripts acceptable at the time of application; official transcripts required upon hire). A curriculum vitae or professional resume, and A list of the three current academic or professional references (please list in the Professional References section of the online application). This position is not eligible for NEW sponsorship. Review of applications will be on a continual basis and will continue until the position(s) are filled. Applicants are retained in the hiring pool for up to two years. Position Details Position Information Announcement Number FAC - VA - 26072 For questions regarding this position, please contact: Frank Kerins Professor fkerins@montana.edu Classification Title Instructor Working Title Finance Instructors for the Jake Jabs College of Business & Entrepreneurship Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) Brief Position Overview The Jake Jabs College of Business and Entrepreneurship offers a Bachelor of Science in Business, with a concentration in finance degree. To accomplish our mission, a significant portion of our teaching faculty should have professional experience in practicing financial management. We seek experienced finance professionals with the ability to teach in more than one area, including financial markets, commercial banking, real estate finance, insurance and risk management, personal finance, investments corporate finance, and derivative securities. Faculty Tenure Track No Faculty Rank Non-Tenure Track Position Number 4A6471 Department Jabs College of Business Instruct Division College of Business Appointment Type Non-Tenure Track (Pooled) Contract Term Academic Year Semester Fall or Spring If other, specify From date If other, specify End date Union Affiliation Contact HR for Determination FTE Varies Benefits Eligible Depends on FTE (please contact Human Resources - 406-994-3651) Salary Salary commensurate with experience, education, and qualifications Contract Type LOA If other, please specify Recruitment Type Open Position Details General Statement Montana State University invites experienced finance professionals to the Jake Jabs College of Business and Entrepreneurship faculty as Instructors, delivering high-quality instruction at the undergraduate and graduate levels. We seek dedicated professionals who are passionate about teaching and mentoring students, possess strong interpersonal and communication skills, and can collaborate effectively with faculty and staff. The ideal candidate will contribute to student success and academic excellence while supporting the mission of Montana State University through engaging, real-world finance education. Instructional assignments are contingent upon departmental needs and the availability of funding. Applications are accepted on a continual basis (unless otherwise indicated) and will be maintained in the pool for up to two years. After two years, candidates will be notified to resubmit their application materials for continued consideration. Application materials will be reviewed by the appropriate search committee or hiring authority, and applicants will be notified if they are being considered for an open position. Non-tenure-track appointments may be part-time or full-time and vary in duration depending on the specific needs of the department or program. Salary is dependent on the number of courses taught and the duration of the appointment. Duties and Responsibilities Teach undergraduate and/or graduate finance courses in on-campus and/or online formats, ensuring high-quality, engaging instruction. Incorporate real-world applications and experiential learning to enhance student understanding of financial principles and practices. Stay current with industry trends, professional standards, and advancements in finance education to maintain course relevance. Foster a welcoming and supportive learning environment. Required Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills Master’s degree in finance or a closely related field. Preferred Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills PhD in finance or a closely related field. Ability to teach undergraduate and/or graduate courses in finance. Industry certification such as CFA , CFP , CMA , CVA , etc. Knowledge of current industry trends and practices in areas such as financial markets, commercial banking, insurance and risk management, real estate finance, personal finance, investments, corporate finance, and derivative securities. The Successful Candidate Will Be committed to experiential learning, incorporating real-world applications, case studies, and industry partnerships into teaching. Be committed to supporting, mentoring, and inspiring students from all backgrounds. Be committed to utilizing effective pedagogy that involves students in the learning process. Have the ability to work well with faculty, staff, and students in a dynamic environment. Position Special Requirements/Additional Information The position for which you have applied MAY BE a Union position. Union affiliation is determined by job duties and the collective bargaining unit. Non-Tenure Track Faculty – Any position that is .5 FTE or more is represented by the Associated Faculty of Montana State University ( AFMSU ). Faculty covered by AFMSU may choose to pay membership dues. This is a condition of employment. Additional information can be found at AFMSU or by emailing AFSMU . Any position less than .5 FTE is not represented by the Union and is not required to pay dues. If the FTE changes during employment, the representational status of this position could be impacted. Exceptions: Anyone having successfully completed a PEI exam or any faculty working in Extension are exempt from the Union. This job description should not be construed as an exhaustive statement of duties, responsibilities or requirements, but a general description of the job. Nothing contained herein restricts Montana State University’s rights to assign or reassign duties and responsibilities to this job at any time. Physical Demands To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. The requirements listed above are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. The Program The Department The College Montana State University is located in Bozeman, MT, an area renowned for its natural beauty and environmental richness. The area offers exceptional school systems, access to art and music, and a myriad of outdoor activities. Montana State University is a Carnegie R1-designated university, hosting scholars from around the world, and the Jake Jabs College of Business & Entrepreneurship is experiencing sustained and unprecedented growth. The finance program offers a finance undergraduate concentration as part of a BS in Business degree. We are dedicated to providing outstanding education for our students and to supporting the scholarship efforts of our faculty. Our College of Business is AACSB -accredited. Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies Multiple Positions Desired Start Date Review of applications will be on a continual basis and will continue until the position(s) are filled. Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Close Date Applications will be: Applications will be accepted and screened for the duration of this pool. Special Instructions Documents required: A letter of application that includes (1) why you are interested in teaching in the finance option in the Jake Jabs College of Business & Entrepreneurship, and (2) what classes/finance topics you are most qualified to teach. A copy of the graduate-level academic transcript (unofficial transcripts acceptable at the time of application; official transcripts required upon hire). A curriculum vitae or professional resume, and A list of the three current academic or professional references (please list in the Professional References section of the online application). This position is not eligible for NEW sponsorship. Review of applications will be on a continual basis and will continue until the position(s) are filled. Applicants are retained in the hiring pool for up to two years. EEO Statement Montana State University is an equal opportunity employer. MSU does not discriminate against any applicant on the basis of race, color, religion, creed, political ideas, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, marital status, national origin, physical or mental disability, or any other protected class status in violation of any applicable law. In compliance with the Montana Veteran’s Employment Preference Act, MSU provides preference in employment to veterans, disabled veterans, and certain eligible relatives of veterans. To claim veteran’s preference, please complete the veteran’s preference information located in the Demographics section of your profile. FLSA Details FLSA Determination FLSA Status Exempt Applicant Documents Required Documents Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae Transcript Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). University Human Resources 920 Technology BLVD, Suite A Bozeman, MT 59718 406-994-3651 humanresources@montana.edu Accessibility | Contact List | Directories | Jobs | Legal & Privacy Policy | Site Index Montana State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/53243": {
      "title": "Extension Agent – Agriculture and 4-H Youth Development – Carbon County",
      "description": "Montana State University Employment Opportunities | Extension Agent – Agriculture and 4-H Youth Development – Carbon County Skip to Main Content Jobs at Montana State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About MSU About Bozeman Benefits Academics Extension Agent – Agriculture and 4-H Youth Development – Carbon County Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This position is not eligible for sponsorship. Please note – for this position – Five (5) references have been requested. Position Details Position Information Announcement Number FAC - VA - 27023 For questions regarding this position, please contact: Tracy Mosley tmosley@montana.edu 406-223-4727 Classification Title Working Title Extension Agent – Agriculture and 4-H Youth Development – Carbon County Brief Position Overview This position is located in Joliet, Montana. The primary duty for County Extension Faculty is to assess local community needs, then to develop, implement, and evaluate Extension programming to meet those needs. The areas of emphasis of this Carbon County Extension Agent position are Agriculture and 4-H Youth Development. The Carbon County Extension office is staffed by one Agriculture and 4-H Youth Development agent, one Family and Consumer Sciences and 4-H Youth Development agent, and three-quarter time administrative assistant. Faculty Tenure Track Yes Faculty Rank Up To Professor Position Number 4B3736 Department Extension Agents/Field Division Extension Appointment Type Faculty Contract Term Fiscal Year Semester If other, specify From date If other, specify End date Union Affiliation Exempt from Collective Bargaining FTE 1.0 Benefits Eligible Eligible Salary MSU Extension is committed to equitable salaries. Starting salaries are determined based on education and prior experience. The minimum base salary with a bachelor’s degree is $51,660, and with a master’s degree is $58,660. Contract Type MUS If other, please specify Recruitment Type Open Position Details General Statement Montana State University ( MSU ) Extension improves the lives of Montana citizens by providing unbiased research-based education and information that integrates learning, discovery, and engagement to strengthen the social, economic and environmental well-being of individuals, families, and communities. MSU Extension is committed to the land grant mission and engaging with communities to address locally identified and statewide needs. MSU Extension has a field faculty staff of 97 Extension Agents serving 56 counties and 7 reservations, and 45 subject matter experts located in Bozeman and other locations across the state. Program offerings include agriculture, horticulture, natural resources, 4-H youth development, family and consumer sciences, and community vitality programs. For additional information see the web site: Extension . Carbon County, located in south-central Montana and created in 1895 from portions of Park and Yellowstone Counties, encompasses 2,066 square miles and is surrounded by the Beartooth Mountains, Pryor Mountains, and Big Horn River. The county population is nearly 11,500, with 2,500 located in the county seat of Red Lodge. Other communities in Carbon County include Bearcreek, Belfry, Boyd, Bridger, Fromberg, Edgar, Joliet, Luther, Roberts, Roscoe, and Silesia. Complete (K-12) school systems exist in the communities of Belfry, Bridger, Fromberg, Joliet, Red Lodge, and Roberts with a K-8 school in Luther. Carbon County is a short distance from Billings, and its economy is based in agriculture, recreation, and tourism. Land distribution includes 17% cropland and 78% pastureland with nearly 99,000 acres irrigated and agriculture consists of predominantly livestock, forages, and small grains. Carbon County 4-H has 187 members and 51 volunteer leaders enrolled in the program and encompasses 8 organized 4-H clubs, as well as archery, shooting sports, and dog project clubs. We seek individuals who work professionally and effectively with various individuals, foster and maintain effective interpersonal relationships, exhibit excellent written and verbal communications skills and have the ability to contribute positively to the Land Grant mission of Montana State University. Duties and Responsibilities Conduct community needs assessment and develop, plan, implement, facilitate, and evaluate successful, research-based educational programs in Agriculture and 4-H Youth Development. Provide shared leadership with the peer Carbon County agent for development, planning, facilitation, and evaluation of the Carbon County 4-H program to foster positive youth development and volunteer engagement. Provide timely, relevant agriculture programming with emphases on livestock and farm/ranch, natural resource, and small acreage management; irrigated and dryland crop production; and horticulture that result in positive community impacts. Build and maintain collaborative working relationships with peer Extension agents, Extension specialists, county commissioners, and appropriate local individuals, groups, boards, agencies, and organizations to leverage educational programming in Carbon County . Collaborate with local and regional Extension staff, community leaders, and stakeholders to conduct needs assessment to identify and inform educational programming priorities in Carbon County. Embrace a team approach to planning, developing, and implementing an effective, interdisciplinary MSU Extension program in Carbon County. Required Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills Bachelor’s degree in agriculture, animal science, agronomy, natural resource management, or a related field . Demonstrated ability to lead groups; assess community needs; and develop, organize, plan, teach, and evaluate effective programs. Demonstrated ability to provide effective leadership for Extension programming for youth, adults, and volunteers. Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively and communicate effectively with individuals, groups, and community organizations representing a wide variety of youth and adult audiences. Preferred Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills Master’s degree. At least one degree or relevant work experience in agriculture, animal science, agronomy, natural resource management, or a related field. Demonstrated ability to facilitate groups and help them find constructive solutions to locally identified issues. Extension experience or demonstrated understanding of the Extension education model. Demonstrated understanding of youth and adult learning principles and their application to community-based education and outreach. Demonstrated ability to recruit, train, and provide professional development to volunteers. The Successful Candidate Will Possess excellent human relation skills. Work with a high level of professionalism. Possess the ability to work effectively with other staff members. Demonstrate evidence of good judgment. Have the flexibility and innovation to respond to changing needs of people in Carbon County. Possess the ability to communicate effectively, both verbally and in writing. Establish relationships and work with various backgrounds and experiences. Ultimately, the successful candidate will be relational, responsive, and reliable. Position Special Requirements/Additional Information If the successful candidate holds a Master’s degree, the position will be filled as a tenure track position. If the successful candidate does not hold a Master’s degree, the position will be filled as a non-tenure track position; however, upon completion of a Master’s degree, they will transition to a tenure track position. Obtain a Government Pesticide Applicator license and provide oversight of the local Private Pesticide Applicator program in Carbon County. Work hours vary and are influenced by community needs. Work outside of normal business hours, including evenings and weekends, is not unusual. Position includes continuous professional development, frequent travel throughout the county, and occasional travel throughout the state of Montana. Must possess a valid driver’s license, an acceptable driving record, and meet all State of Montana requirements to operate State/University vehicles. (If successful candidate possesses a valid out-of-state driver’s license, must obtain a valid Montana driver’s license within 60 days of hire.) This job description should not be construed as an exhaustive statement of duties, responsibilities or requirements, but a general description of the job. Nothing contained herein restricts Montana State University’s rights to assign or reassign duties and responsibilities to this job at any time. Physical Demands To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. The requirements listed above are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. The Program The Department The College Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date Upon completion of a successful search Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Close Date Applications will be: Screening of applications will begin on October 30, 2026 ; however, applications will continue to be accepted until an adequate applicant pool has been established. Special Instructions This position is not eligible for sponsorship. Please note – for this position – Five (5) references have been requested. EEO Statement Montana State University is an equal opportunity employer. MSU does not discriminate against any applicant on the basis of race, color, religion, creed, political ideas, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, marital status, national origin, physical or mental disability, or any other protected class status in violation of any applicable law. In compliance with the Montana Veteran’s Employment Preference Act, MSU provides preference in employment to veterans, disabled veterans, and certain eligible relatives of veterans. To claim veteran’s preference, please complete the veteran’s preference information located in the Demographics section of your profile. FLSA Details FLSA Determination FLSA Status Exempt Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter addressing each of the Required and Preferred Qualifications Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). University Human Resources 920 Technology BLVD, Suite A Bozeman, MT 59718 406-994-3651 humanresources@montana.edu Accessibility | Contact List | Directories | Jobs | Legal & Privacy Policy | Site Index Montana State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/53242": {
      "title": "Extension Agent – Agriculture, Natural Resources, and 4-H Youth Development – Fergus and Petroleum Counties",
      "description": "Montana State University Employment Opportunities | Extension Agent – Agriculture, Natural Resources, and 4-H Youth Development – Fergus and Petroleum Counties Skip to Main Content Jobs at Montana State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About MSU About Bozeman Benefits Academics Extension Agent – Agriculture, Natural Resources, and 4-H Youth Development – Fergus and Petroleum Counties Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This position is not eligible for sponsorship. Please note – for this position – Five (5) references have been requested. Position Details Position Information Announcement Number FAC - VA - 27022 For questions regarding this position, please contact: Tracy Mosley tmosley@montana.edu 406-223-4727 Classification Title Working Title Extension Agent – Agriculture, Natural Resources, and 4-H Youth Development – Fergus and Petroleum Counties Brief Position Overview This position is located in Lewistown, Montana. The primary duty for County Extension Faculty is to assess local community needs, then to develop, implement, and evaluate Extension programming to meet those needs. The primary areas of emphasis of this Fergus-Petroleum Counties Extension Agent position are Agriculture, Natural Resources and 4-H Youth Development, with secondary emphasis on Community Vitality. The Fergus-Petroleum Counties Extension office is staffed by one Agriculture, Natural Resources, and 4-H Youth Development agent; one Family and Consumer Sciences and 4-H Youth Development agent, one 4-H Program Assistant, and one full-time administrative assistant. Faculty Tenure Track Yes Faculty Rank Up To Professor Position Number 4B3914 Department Extension Agents/Field Division Extension Appointment Type Faculty Contract Term Fiscal Year Semester If other, specify From date If other, specify End date Union Affiliation Exempt from Collective Bargaining FTE 1.0 Benefits Eligible Eligible Salary MSU Extension is committed to equitable salaries. Starting salaries are determined based on education and prior experience. The minimum base salary with a bachelor’s degree is $51,660, and with a master’s degree is $58,660. Contract Type MUS If other, please specify Recruitment Type Open Position Details General Statement Montana State University ( MSU ) Extension improves the lives of Montana citizens by providing unbiased research-based education and information that integrates learning, discovery, and engagement to strengthen the social, economic and environmental well-being of individuals, families, and communities. MSU Extension is committed to the land grant mission and engaging with communities to address locally identified and statewide needs. MSU Extension has a field faculty staff of 97 Extension Agents serving 56 counties and 7 reservations, and 45 subject matter experts located in Bozeman and other locations across the state. Program offerings include agriculture, horticulture, natural resources, 4-H youth development, family and consumer sciences, and community vitality programs. For additional information see the web site: Extension . Fergus and Petroleum Counties, located in Central Montana, encompass just over 6,200 square miles and are populated by approximately 11,800 and 550 residents, respectively. The county seats of Lewistown and Winnett have approximately 6,200 and 200 residents, respectively. Other towns include Denton, Grass Range, Moore, Roy, and Winifred. Excellent schools and the Central Montana Medical Center are important aspects of this area, as are the multitude of recreational activities available across the varied landscape and streams. Agriculture is a primary economic driver in both counties, dominated by livestock, hay, and small grain production, with most of the land in pastures and cropland. The Fergus-Petroleum Counties 4-H program has 236 members and 76 volunteer leaders enrolled in the program and encompasses 13 organized 4-H clubs. We seek individuals who work professionally and effectively with various individuals, foster and maintain effective interpersonal relationships, exhibit excellent written and verbal communications skills and have the ability to contribute positively to the Land Grant mission of Montana State University. Duties and Responsibilities Conduct community needs assessment and develop, plan, implement, facilitate, and evaluate successful, research-based educational programs in Agriculture, Natural Resources, and Horticulture; 4-H Youth Development; and Community Vitality. Provide shared leadership with the peer Fergus and Petroleum Counties agent for development, planning, facilitation, and evaluation of the Fergus and Petroleum Counties 4-H program to foster positive youth development and volunteer engagement. Provide timely, relevant agriculture programming focused on livestock production; natural resource, farm and ranch, small acreage, and weed management; and horticulture that results in positive community impacts. Build and maintain collaborative working relationships with peer Extension agents, Extension specialists, county commissioners, and appropriate local individuals, groups, boards, agencies, and organizations to leverage educational programming in Fergus and Petroleum Counties . Work collaboratively with Fergus County Human Resources and the Commissioners to hire, supervise, support, and coach county employees in the Extension Office. Collaborate with local and regional Extension staff, community leaders, and stakeholders to conduct needs assessment to identify and inform educational programming priorities in Fergus and Petroleum Counties. Embrace a team approach to planning, developing, and implementing an effective, interdisciplinary MSU Extension program in Fergus and Petroleum Counties. Required Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills Bachelor’s degree in agriculture, animal science, natural resource management, or a related field. Demonstrated ability to lead groups; assess community needs; and develop, organize, plan, teach, and evaluate effective programs. Demonstrated ability to provide effective leadership for Extension programming for youth, adults, and volunteers. Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively and communicate effectively with individuals, groups, and community organizations representing a wide variety of youth and adult audiences. Preferred Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills Master’s degree. At least one degree or relevant work experience in agriculture, animal science, natural resource management, or a related field. Demonstrated ability to facilitate groups and help them find constructive solutions to locally identified issues. Extension experience or demonstrated understanding of the Extension education model. Demonstrated understanding of youth and adult learning principles and their application to community-based education and outreach. Demonstrated ability to recruit, train, and provide professional development to volunteers. The Successful Candidate Will Possess excellent human relation skills. Work with a high level of professionalism. Possess the ability to work effectively with other staff members. Demonstrate evidence of good judgment. Have the flexibility and innovation to respond to changing needs of people in Fergus and Petroleum Counties. Possess the ability to communicate effectively, both verbally and in writing. Establish relationships and work with various backgrounds and experiences. Ultimately, the successful candidate will be relational, responsive, and reliable. Position Special Requirements/Additional Information If the successful candidate holds a Master’s degree, the position will be filled as a tenure track position. If the successful candidate does not hold a Master’s degree, the position will be filled as a non-tenure track position; however, upon completion of a Master’s degree, they will transition to a tenure track position. Obtain a Government Pesticide Applicator license and provide oversight of the local Private Pesticide Applicator program in Fergus and Petroleum Counties. Work hours vary and are influenced by community needs. Work outside of normal business hours, including evenings and weekends, is not unusual. Position includes continuous professional development, frequent travel throughout the county, and occasional travel throughout the state of Montana. Must possess a valid driver’s license, an acceptable driving record, and meet all State of Montana requirements to operate State/University vehicles. (If successful candidate possesses a valid out-of-state driver’s license, must obtain a valid Montana driver’s license within 60 days of hire.) This job description should not be construed as an exhaustive statement of duties, responsibilities or requirements, but a general description of the job. Nothing contained herein restricts Montana State University’s rights to assign or reassign duties and responsibilities to this job at any time. Physical Demands To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. The requirements listed above are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. The Program The Department The College Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date Upon completion of a successful search Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Close Date Applications will be: Screening of applications will begin on October 30, 2026 ; however, applications will continue to be accepted until an adequate applicant pool has been established. Special Instructions This position is not eligible for sponsorship. Please note – for this position – Five (5) references have been requested. EEO Statement Montana State University is an equal opportunity employer. MSU does not discriminate against any applicant on the basis of race, color, religion, creed, political ideas, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, marital status, national origin, physical or mental disability, or any other protected class status in violation of any applicable law. In compliance with the Montana Veteran’s Employment Preference Act, MSU provides preference in employment to veterans, disabled veterans, and certain eligible relatives of veterans. To claim veteran’s preference, please complete the veteran’s preference information located in the Demographics section of your profile. FLSA Details FLSA Determination FLSA Status Exempt Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter addressing each of the Required and Preferred Qualifications Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). University Human Resources 920 Technology BLVD, Suite A Bozeman, MT 59718 406-994-3651 humanresources@montana.edu Accessibility | Contact List | Directories | Jobs | Legal & Privacy Policy | Site Index Montana State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/53235": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Mathematics Education",
      "description": "Montana State University Employment Opportunities | Assistant Professor of Mathematics Education Skip to Main Content Jobs at Montana State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About MSU About Bozeman Benefits Academics Assistant Professor of Mathematics Education Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. As part of your application, please upload the following required documents: Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter addressing each of the Required and Preferred Qualifications Research Statement (max 3 pages) Teaching Statement (max 3 pages) References and Letters of Recommendation : All applicants will be required to provide a minimum of three references during the application process, including one reference who can speak to the candidate’s teaching ability. Following the initial application screening, references for candidates moving forward to initial interviews will be contacted by email to request a letter of recommendation. References may also be contacted by phone as part of the final reference check process. Position Details Position Information Announcement Number FAC - VA - 27021 For questions regarding this position, please contact: Molly Patten Business Operations Manager molly.patten@montana.edu Classification Title Working Title Assistant Professor of Mathematics Education Brief Position Overview The Department of Mathematical Sciences at Montana State University ( MSU ) invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Mathematics Education, to begin August 2027. We seek candidates whose research, teaching, and outreach are aligned with secondary mathematics education. We are excited to welcome a new colleague who shares our vision of empowering human beings to think quantitatively and generate new knowledge in the mathematical sciences. Faculty Tenure Track Yes Faculty Rank Assistant Professor Position Number 4A3448 Department Mathematical Sciences Division College of Letters & Science Appointment Type Faculty Contract Term Academic Year Semester If other, specify From date If other, specify End date Union Affiliation Exempt from Collective Bargaining FTE 1.0 Benefits Eligible Eligible Salary Salary commensurate with experience, education, and qualifications Contract Type MUS If other, please specify Recruitment Type Open Position Details General Statement Montana State University is a land-grant institution committed to achievement in research. The Department of Mathematical Sciences has a lively research culture, including M.S. and Ph.D. programs in Mathematics and Statistics. The faculty in the department comprises three disciplinary groups: Mathematics, Statistics, and Mathematics Education. The mathematics education group includes specialists in secondary, elementary, and middle grades mathematics education. We maintain a strong commitment to conducting research in K-12 mathematics education, teaching excellence in undergraduate and graduate mathematics and mathematics education courses and strengthening K-12 mathematics education through professional development and outreach at the state and national levels. We are seeking a candidate who demonstrates commitment to the mathematical preparation of secondary teachers. We seek individuals who work professionally and effectively with individuals from all backgrounds, possess effective interpersonal, written and verbal communication skills and have the ability to contribute positively to the academic success of the students and the mission of Montana State University. Duties and Responsibilities Duties include research, teaching, and service. A commitment to excellence in teaching and an active research program are essential. Research responsibilities include conducting a research program that results in publication in high-quality venues and seeking external funding for research and projects. Instructional responsibilities include teaching lower division, upper division, and graduate courses in the mathematics education program, with a focus on mathematics content courses. These responsibilities include teaching online and in-person courses for practicing teachers through the M.S. in Mathematics with an option in Mathematics Education, additional compensation is provided for summer courses. The candidate may also be expected to supervise mathematics education and mathematics courses. The candidate will advise graduate and undergraduate students and serve on master’s and doctoral committees. Service responsibilities include department, college, and university committee work, outreach to the Montana education community, and participation in professional organizations. Required Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills Ph.D. in Mathematics Education or in the mathematical sciences with a research program focused on secondary mathematics education by start date. Master’s degree in mathematical sciences, or the equivalent, with appropriate coursework in applied or theoretical mathematics or statistics. Demonstrated research potential in mathematics education with a research specialty aligned with secondary mathematics education. Demonstrated teaching potential in mathematics. Demonstrated potential to mentor and advise undergraduate and graduate students. Preferred Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills An active research program in mathematics education with a research specialty aligned with secondary mathematics education. Demonstrated experience working with pre-service or in-service secondary mathematics teacher programs, or experience teaching mathematics at the secondary level. Demonstrated potential to develop an independent research program. Demonstrated potential to secure external research funding. Demonstrated experience teaching at the lower-division, upper-division, and graduate levels. Demonstrated experience mentoring students, particularly at the graduate level. Experience or interest in interdisciplinary collaboration with researchers in other scientific disciplines. The Successful Candidate Will Contribute to the department’s mission of providing outstanding teaching, research, and service, guided by the principle of using disciplinary tools to advance human flourishing. Possess strong oral and written communication skills and effective interpersonal skills. Collaborate effectively with students and faculty at MSU and with researchers across disciplines. Be committed to the mathematical preparation of secondary teachers. Be committed to working with and engaging students and colleagues from all backgrounds within and beyond the department. Position Special Requirements/Additional Information Ph.D. must be earned by August 14, 2027. To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. The requirements listed above are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. Physical Demands To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. The requirements listed above are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. The Program The Department The Department of Mathematical Sciences is recognized as a leading department of Mathematics, Statistics, and Mathematics Education. Bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral graduates in all of these areas are following successful careers in industry, government, and academia. Located in the heart of the Rocky Mountains, 80 miles north of Yellowstone National Park, we offer outstanding educational opportunities in an area of exquisitely beautiful scenery and outdoor recreation. Our department has a multifaceted role on campus and in Montana. We have the largest instructional component on campus, delivering about 10% of the total student credit hours. We offer a B.S. in Mathematics with options in mathematics, applied mathematics, mathematics teaching, and statistics; an M.S. in Mathematics with options in Mathematics and Mathematics Education; an M.S. in Statistics; a Ph.D. in Mathematics and a Ph.D. in Mathematics with an emphasis in Mathematics Education; and a Ph.D. in Statistics. The mathematics education option for the M.S. in Mathematics is an online program. The College The College of Letters and Science ( CLS ), the largest center for learning, teaching and research at Montana State University, offers students an excellent liberal arts and sciences education in nearly 50 majors, 25 minors and over 25 graduate degrees within the four areas of the humanities, social sciences, natural and physical sciences, and mathematical sciences. Building on the great strength of our traditional disciplines, the college provides exciting opportunities for faculty and students at the cutting edge of interdisciplinary inquiry. CLS is dedicated to supporting student success, discovering and disseminating new knowledge, and providing an atmosphere in which discovery and learning are integrated and valued. CLS is at the confluence of intellectual tradition, discovery, and innovation. Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date August 2027 Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Close Date Applications will be: Screening of applications will begin on November 2, 2026 ; however, applications will continue to be accepted until an adequate applicant pool has been established. Special Instructions As part of your application, please upload the following required documents: Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter addressing each of the Required and Preferred Qualifications Research Statement (max 3 pages) Teaching Statement (max 3 pages) References and Letters of Recommendation : All applicants will be required to provide a minimum of three references during the application process, including one reference who can speak to the candidate’s teaching ability. Following the initial application screening, references for candidates moving forward to initial interviews will be contacted by email to request a letter of recommendation. References may also be contacted by phone as part of the final reference check process. EEO Statement Montana State University is an equal opportunity employer. MSU does not discriminate against any applicant on the basis of race, color, religion, creed, political ideas, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, marital status, national origin, physical or mental disability, or any other protected class status in violation of any applicable law. In compliance with the Montana Veteran’s Employment Preference Act, MSU provides preference in employment to veterans, disabled veterans, and certain eligible relatives of veterans. To claim veteran’s preference, please complete the veteran’s preference information located in the Demographics section of your profile. FLSA Details FLSA Determination FLSA Status Exempt Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter addressing each of the Required and Preferred Qualifications Research Statement Teaching Statement Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). University Human Resources 920 Technology BLVD, Suite A Bozeman, MT 59718 406-994-3651 humanresources@montana.edu Accessibility | Contact List | Directories | Jobs | Legal & Privacy Policy | Site Index Montana State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/53231": {
      "title": "Accounting Instructors for the Jake Jabs College of Business &amp; Entrepreneurship Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool)",
      "description": "Montana State University Employment Opportunities | Accounting Instructors for the Jake Jabs College of Business &amp; Entrepreneurship Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) Skip to Main Content Jobs at Montana State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About MSU About Bozeman Benefits Academics Accounting Instructors for the Jake Jabs College of Business & Entrepreneurship Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Documents required: A letter of application that includes (1) why you are interested in teaching in the accounting option at the Jake Jabs College of Business & Entrepreneurship, and (2) what classes/accounting topics you are most qualified to teach. A copy of the graduate-level academic transcript (unofficial transcripts acceptable at the time of application; official transcripts required upon hire). A curriculum vitae or professional resume, and A list of the three current academic or professional references (please list in the Professional References section of the online application). This position is not eligible for NEW sponsorship. Review of applications will be on a continual basis and will continue until the position(s) are filled. Applicants are retained in the hiring pool for up to two years. Position Details Position Information Announcement Number FAC - VA - 26076 For questions regarding this position, please contact: Frank Kerins Professor fkerins@montana.edu Classification Title Instructor Working Title Accounting Instructors for the Jake Jabs College of Business & Entrepreneurship Non-Tenure Track Faculty (Applicant Pool) Brief Position Overview The Jake Jabs College of Business and Entrepreneurship offers a Bachelor of Science in Business, with a concentration in accounting degree. To accomplish our mission, a significant portion of our teaching faculty should have professional experience in practicing accounting. We seek experienced accounting professionals with the ability to teach in one or more accounting areas, including tax, data analytics, cost/managerial accounting, governmental/nonprofit accounting, financial accounting, fraud examination, and auditing. Faculty Tenure Track No Faculty Rank Non-Tenure Track Position Number 4A6471 Department Jabs College of Business Instruct Division College of Business Appointment Type Non-Tenure Track (Pooled) Contract Term Academic Year Semester Fall or Spring If other, specify From date If other, specify End date Union Affiliation Contact HR for Determination FTE Varies Benefits Eligible Depends on FTE (please contact Human Resources - 406-994-3651) Salary Salary commensurate with experience, education, and qualifications Contract Type LOA If other, please specify Recruitment Type Open Position Details General Statement Montana State University invites experienced accounting professionals to the Jake Jabs College of Business and Entrepreneurship faculty as Instructors, delivering high-quality instruction at the undergraduate and graduate levels. We seek dedicated professionals who are passionate about teaching and mentoring students, possess strong interpersonal and communication skills, and can collaborate effectively with faculty and staff. The ideal candidate will contribute to student success and academic excellence while supporting the mission of Montana State University through engaging, real-world accounting education. Instructional assignments are contingent upon departmental needs and the availability of funding. Applications are accepted on a continual basis (unless otherwise indicated) and will be maintained in the pool for up to two years. After two years, candidates will be notified to resubmit their application materials for continued consideration. Application materials will be reviewed by the appropriate search committee or hiring authority, and applicants will be notified if they are being considered for an open position. Non-tenure-track appointments may be part-time or full-time and vary in duration depending on the specific needs of the department or program. Salary is dependent on the number of courses taught and the duration of the appointment. Duties and Responsibilities Teach undergraduate and/or graduate accounting courses in on-campus and/or online formats, ensuring high-quality, engaging instruction. Incorporate real-world applications and experiential learning to enhance student understanding of accounting principles and practices. Stay current with industry trends, professional standards, and advancements in accounting education to maintain course relevance. Foster a welcoming and supportive learning environment. Required Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills Master’s degree in Accounting, Business Administration, or a closely related field from an accredited institution. Preferred Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills Relevant accounting certification ( CPA , CMA , CIA , CFE , etc.). Ph.D. in Accounting, Business Administration, or a closely related field from an accredited institution. Demonstrated ability to teach undergraduate and/or graduate courses in accounting. Knowledge of current industry trends and practices in areas such as tax, data analytics, cost/managerial accounting, governmental/nonprofit accounting, financial accounting, fraud examination, and auditing. The Successful Candidate Will Be committed to experiential learning, incorporating real-world applications, case studies, and industry partnerships into teaching. Be committed to supporting, mentoring, and inspiring students from all backgrounds. Be committed to utilizing effective pedagogy that involves students in the learning process. Have the ability to work well with faculty, staff, and students in a dynamic environment. Position Special Requirements/Additional Information The position for which you have applied MAY BE a Union position. Union affiliation is determined by job duties and the collective bargaining unit. Non-Tenure Track Faculty – Any position that is .5 FTE or more is represented by the Associated Faculty of Montana State University ( AFMSU ). Faculty covered by AFMSU may choose to pay membership dues. This is a condition of employment. Additional information can be found at AFMSU or by emailing AFSMU . Any position less than .5 FTE is not represented by the Union and is not required to pay dues. If the FTE changes during employment, the representational status of this position could be impacted. Exceptions: Anyone having successfully completed a PEI exam or any faculty working in Extension are exempt from the Union. This job description should not be construed as an exhaustive statement of duties, responsibilities or requirements, but a general description of the job. Nothing contained herein restricts Montana State University’s rights to assign or reassign duties and responsibilities to this job at any time. Physical Demands To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. The requirements listed above are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. The Program The Department The College Montana State University is located in Bozeman, MT, an area renowned for its natural beauty and environmental richness. The area offers exceptional school systems, access to art and music, and a myriad of outdoor activities. Montana State University is a Carnegie R1-designated university, hosting scholars from around the world, and the Jake Jabs College of Business & Entrepreneurship is experiencing sustained and unprecedented growth. The accounting program offers an accounting undergraduate concentration as part of a BS in Business degree, and a Master of Professional Accountancy degree. We are dedicated to providing outstanding education for our students and to supporting the scholarship efforts of our faculty. Our College of Business is AACSB -accredited. Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies Multiple Positions Desired Start Date Review of applications will be on a continual basis and will continue until the position(s) are filled. Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Close Date Applications will be: Applications will be accepted and screened for the duration of this pool. Special Instructions Documents required: A letter of application that includes (1) why you are interested in teaching in the accounting option at the Jake Jabs College of Business & Entrepreneurship, and (2) what classes/accounting topics you are most qualified to teach. A copy of the graduate-level academic transcript (unofficial transcripts acceptable at the time of application; official transcripts required upon hire). A curriculum vitae or professional resume, and A list of the three current academic or professional references (please list in the Professional References section of the online application). This position is not eligible for NEW sponsorship. Review of applications will be on a continual basis and will continue until the position(s) are filled. Applicants are retained in the hiring pool for up to two years. EEO Statement Montana State University is an equal opportunity employer. MSU does not discriminate against any applicant on the basis of race, color, religion, creed, political ideas, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, marital status, national origin, physical or mental disability, or any other protected class status in violation of any applicable law. In compliance with the Montana Veteran’s Employment Preference Act, MSU provides preference in employment to veterans, disabled veterans, and certain eligible relatives of veterans. To claim veteran’s preference, please complete the veteran’s preference information located in the Demographics section of your profile. FLSA Details FLSA Determination FLSA Status Exempt Applicant Documents Required Documents Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae Transcript Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). University Human Resources 920 Technology BLVD, Suite A Bozeman, MT 59718 406-994-3651 humanresources@montana.edu Accessibility | Contact List | Directories | Jobs | Legal & Privacy Policy | Site Index Montana State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/53206": {
      "title": "College of Nursing Cohort - Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Montana State University Employment Opportunities | College of Nursing Cohort - Assistant Professor Skip to Main Content Jobs at Montana State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About MSU About Bozeman Benefits Academics College of Nursing Cohort - Assistant Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This position is not eligible for NEW sponsorship. To apply, submit the following: A cover letter addressing each of the required and preferred qualifications in the order listed above. A complete curriculum vitae including relevant work and teaching experience. References: Please indicate to which of the following they will be able to speak: teaching, research, service or practice. Position Details Position Information Announcement Number FAC - VA - 27013 For questions regarding this position, please contact: Dr. Tracy Hellem tracy.hellem1@montana.edu (406) 994-2149 Classification Title Working Title College of Nursing Cohort - Assistant Professor Brief Position Overview The Mark and Robyn Jones College of Nursing is searching to make a cohort hire of assistant professor tenure-track faculty with primary responsibilities teaching both undergraduate and graduate courses in nursing, developing and/or sustaining a funded program of research, and participating in professional/service activities. Faculty Tenure Track Yes Faculty Rank Assistant Professor Position Number 4A4168/4A5236 Department Nursing Departments Division College of Nursing Appointment Type Faculty Contract Term Academic Year Semester If other, specify From date If other, specify End date Union Affiliation Exempt from Collective Bargaining FTE 1.0 Benefits Eligible Eligible Salary $80,000 annually, commensurate with experience, education, and qualifications Contract Type MUS If other, please specify Recruitment Type Open Position Details General Statement Make history and join our college in transforming nursing education and healthcare in Montana! Through the generous philanthropic investment of $101 million from Mark and Robyn Jones , the founders of Goosehead Insurance, we have constructed five new nursing education buildings (one on each of the nursing campuses), expanded our endowed professorships and student scholarships, and started Montana’s first Nurse Midwifery program. The Mark and Robyn Jones College of Nursing ( MRJCON ) offers a baccalaureate in nursing, accelerated baccalaureate in nursing, Master of Nursing focused on clinical leadership, and Doctor of Nursing Practice with focus as a family nurse practitioner, psych-mental health nurse practitioner, or nurse-midwife. The College has five campus locations across the state, located in Billings, Bozeman, Great Falls, Kalispell, and Missoula. The Mark and Robyn Jones College of Nursing is seeking to hire 3-7 assistant professors as a cohort to start January 1, 2027. Faculty representing a variety of backgrounds to assume tenure track positions in various specialty areas are sought. Faculty members have opportunities to teach in both the graduate and undergraduate programs. Tenure track faculty members are expected to establish a focused program of research relevant to Montana and to successfully seek extramural funding. All members of the faculty are expected to engage in college and university service and to provide nursing leadership in Montana and beyond through active participation in professional nursing organizations. We hope to attract applicants who are committed to helping students from different backgrounds succeed. Duties and Responsibilities The Mark and Robyn Jones College of Nursing is seeking nursing faculty to assume tenure track positions in a variety of specialty areas. Faculty members have opportunities to teach in both the graduate and undergraduate programs. Tenure track faculty members are expected to establish a focused program of research relevant to Montana and to successfully seek extramural funding. All members of the faculty are expected to engage in professional/college/university service and to provide nursing leadership in Montana and beyond through active participation in professional nursing organizations. We hope to attract applicants who are committed to helping students from many backgrounds succeed. For more information please see the College of Nursing Policy E-1 https://www.montana.edu/provost/faculty/MRJCONRS7.1.26.pdf Required Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills Doctorate in nursing or related field ( ABD nearing completion may be considered). Record of or demonstrable potential for excellence in teaching. Record of excellence or demonstrable potential for excellence in research/scholarship in an area of direct applicability to the college of nursing. Evidence of strong written communication skills. Evidence of service to the nursing profession/nursing education/rural nursing Preferred Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills Graduate degree in nursing or related field. Eligibility for RN licensure in Montana. Teaching experience at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Experience with simulation pedagogy and distance delivery of education. Demonstrated potential or ability to work collaboratively in interdisciplinary teams. Potential to foster and support student and faculty of many backgrounds. The Successful Candidate Will The successful applicant will be committed to excellence in teaching nursing courses as well as in developing a program of funded research that is directly relevant to nursing profession and in disseminating that work through peer-reviewed publications. Additionally, this individual will demonstrate the commitment to being a collaborative team member in the College, to supporting the mission of the College, and to working in a collegial manner with health care professionals external to the university. Applicants will be required to actively participate in activities related to cohort-hire success including research training, regular group and individual mentoring meetings, and writing retreats. Position Special Requirements/Additional Information This position is not eligible for NEW sponsorship. This job description should not be construed as an exhaustive statement of duties, responsibilities or requirements, but a general description of the job. Nothing contained herein restricts Montana State University’s rights to assign or reassign duties and responsibilities to this job at any time. Physical Demands To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. The requirements listed above are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. The Program The Department The College Welcome to the Mark and Robyn Jones College of Nursing. We are very proud of both the academic programs and vibrant educational community that we have developed. Specifically, we value our student-friendly environment, outstanding faculty and the resulting success of our students. We provide our undergraduate curriculum in-person in five locations across the state and deliver our graduate program using distance delivery strategies to better serve the needs of our students and the Montana health care system and communities. Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 3-7 Desired Start Date January 1, 2027 Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Close Date Applications will be: Screening of applications will begin on October 15, 2026 ; however, applications will continue to be accepted until an adequate applicant pool has been established. Special Instructions This position is not eligible for NEW sponsorship. To apply, submit the following: A cover letter addressing each of the required and preferred qualifications in the order listed above. A complete curriculum vitae including relevant work and teaching experience. References: Please indicate to which of the following they will be able to speak: teaching, research, service or practice. EEO Statement Montana State University is an equal opportunity employer. MSU does not discriminate against any applicant on the basis of race, color, religion, creed, political ideas, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, marital status, national origin, physical or mental disability, or any other protected class status in violation of any applicable law. In compliance with the Montana Veteran’s Employment Preference Act, MSU provides preference in employment to veterans, disabled veterans, and certain eligible relatives of veterans. To claim veteran’s preference, please complete the veteran’s preference information located in the Demographics section of your profile. FLSA Details FLSA Determination FLSA Status Exempt Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter addressing each of the Required and Preferred Qualifications Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). University Human Resources 920 Technology BLVD, Suite A Bozeman, MT 59718 406-994-3651 humanresources@montana.edu Accessibility | Contact List | Directories | Jobs | Legal & Privacy Policy | Site Index Montana State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/53203": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Mathematics",
      "description": "Montana State University Employment Opportunities | Assistant Professor of Mathematics Skip to Main Content Jobs at Montana State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About MSU About Bozeman Benefits Academics Assistant Professor of Mathematics Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. As part of your application, please upload the following required documents: Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter addressing each of the Required and Preferred Qualifications Research Statement (max 3 pages) Teaching Statement (max 3 pages) References and Letters of Recommendation: All applicants will be required to provide a minimum of three references during the application process, including one reference who can speak to the candidate’s teaching ability. References will be contacted automatically by email once the application is submitted to request a letter of recommendation. Applicants should notify their references in advance and let them know that letters must be submitted by the screening date . References may also be contacted by phone as part of the final reference check process. Position Details Position Information Announcement Number FAC - VA - 27020 For questions regarding this position, please contact: Molly Patten Business Operations Manager molly.patten@montana.edu Classification Title Working Title Assistant Professor of Mathematics Brief Position Overview The Department of Mathematical Sciences at Montana State University ( MSU ) invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Mathematics, to begin August 2027. We seek candidates who are broadly trained in applied mathematics and who have a commitment to excellence in teaching. We seek colleagues with research interests in any area of applied mathematics, including computational and applied mathematics, mathematical biology, modeling and analysis of complex data and physical systems, mathematical optimization, machine learning, or data science. Faculty Tenure Track Yes Faculty Rank Assistant Professor Position Number 4A3327 Department Mathematical Sciences Division College of Letters & Science Appointment Type Faculty Contract Term Academic Year Semester If other, specify From date If other, specify End date Union Affiliation Exempt from Collective Bargaining FTE 1.0 Benefits Eligible Eligible Salary Salary commensurate with experience, education, and qualifications Contract Type MUS If other, please specify Recruitment Type Open Position Details General Statement Montana State University is a land-grant institution committed to achievement in research. The Department of Mathematical Sciences has a lively research culture, including M.S. and Ph.D. programs in Mathematics and Statistics. The faculty in the department comprises three disciplinary groups: Mathematics, Statistics, and Mathematics Education. The mathematics group includes both pure and applied mathematicians, with research areas ranging from mathematical biology, numerical PDEs, and optimization, to quantum topology, mathematical physics, complex analysis, and dynamical systems. We seek candidates who will complement and extend these research areas. We seek individuals who work professionally and effectively with individuals from all backgrounds, possess effective interpersonal, written and verbal communication skills and have the ability to contribute positively to the academic success of the students and the mission of Montana State University. Duties and Responsibilities Duties include research, teaching, and service. A commitment to excellence in teaching and an active research program are essential. Research responsibilities include conducting a research program that results in publication in high-quality venues and seeking external funding for research and projects. Instructional responsibilities include teaching lower division, upper division, and graduate courses in mathematics, as well as advising undergraduate and graduate students and supervising lower division courses. Service includes department, college, and university committee work, consulting with university scientists, and participation in local and national professional organizations. Required Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills Ph.D. in mathematics or a closely related field by start date. Demonstrated research potential in computational or applied mathematics. Demonstrated teaching potential in mathematics. Demonstrated potential to mentor and advise undergraduate and graduate students. Preferred Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills An active research program in computational or applied mathematics. Demonstrated potential to develop an independent research program. Demonstrated potential to secure external research funding. Demonstrated experience teaching at the lower-division, upper-division, and graduate levels. Demonstrated experience mentoring students, particularly at the graduate level. Experience or interest in interdisciplinary collaboration with researchers in other scientific disciplines. The Successful Candidate Will Contribute to the department’s mission of providing outstanding teaching, research, and service, guided by the principle of using disciplinary tools to advance human flourishing. Possess strong oral and written communication skills and effective interpersonal skills. Collaborate effectively with students and faculty at MSU and with researchers across disciplines. Be committed to working with and engaging students and colleagues from all backgrounds within and beyond the department. Position Special Requirements/Additional Information Ph.D. must be earned by August 14, 2027. To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. The requirements listed above are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. Physical Demands To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. The requirements listed above are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. The Program The Department The Department of Mathematical Sciences is recognized as a leading department of Mathematics, Statistics, and Mathematics Education. Bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral graduates in all of these areas are following successful careers in industry, government, and academia. Located in the heart of the Rocky Mountains, 80 miles north of Yellowstone National Park, we offer outstanding educational opportunities in an area of exquisitely beautiful scenery and outdoor recreation. Our department has a multifaceted role on campus and in Montana. We have the largest instructional component on campus, delivering about 10% of the total student credit hours. We offer a B.S. in Mathematics with options in mathematics, applied mathematics, mathematics teaching, and statistics; an M.S. in Mathematics with options in Mathematics and Mathematics Education; an M.S. in Statistics; a Ph.D. in Mathematics and a Ph.D. in Mathematics with an emphasis in Mathematics Education; and a Ph.D. in Statistics. The mathematics education option for the M.S. in Mathematics is an online program. The College The College of Letters and Science ( CLS ), the largest center for learning, teaching and research at Montana State University, offers students an excellent liberal arts and sciences education in nearly 50 majors, 25 minors and over 25 graduate degrees within the four areas of the humanities, social sciences, natural and physical sciences, and mathematical sciences. Building on the great strength of our traditional disciplines, the college provides exciting opportunities for faculty and students at the cutting edge of interdisciplinary inquiry. CLS is dedicated to supporting student success, discovering and disseminating new knowledge, and providing an atmosphere in which discovery and learning are integrated and valued. CLS is at the confluence of intellectual tradition, discovery, and innovation. Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date August 2027 Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Close Date Applications will be: Screening of applications will begin on November 2, 2026 ; however, applications will continue to be accepted until an adequate applicant pool has been established. Special Instructions As part of your application, please upload the following required documents: Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter addressing each of the Required and Preferred Qualifications Research Statement (max 3 pages) Teaching Statement (max 3 pages) References and Letters of Recommendation: All applicants will be required to provide a minimum of three references during the application process, including one reference who can speak to the candidate’s teaching ability. References will be contacted automatically by email once the application is submitted to request a letter of recommendation. Applicants should notify their references in advance and let them know that letters must be submitted by the screening date . References may also be contacted by phone as part of the final reference check process. EEO Statement Montana State University is an equal opportunity employer. MSU does not discriminate against any applicant on the basis of race, color, religion, creed, political ideas, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, marital status, national origin, physical or mental disability, or any other protected class status in violation of any applicable law. In compliance with the Montana Veteran’s Employment Preference Act, MSU provides preference in employment to veterans, disabled veterans, and certain eligible relatives of veterans. To claim veteran’s preference, please complete the veteran’s preference information located in the Demographics section of your profile. FLSA Details FLSA Determination FLSA Status Exempt Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter addressing each of the Required and Preferred Qualifications Research Statement Teaching Statement Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). University Human Resources 920 Technology BLVD, Suite A Bozeman, MT 59718 406-994-3651 humanresources@montana.edu Accessibility | Contact List | Directories | Jobs | Legal & Privacy Policy | Site Index Montana State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
